WEBVTT

00:00:06.938 --> 00:00:11.443
At the sea side.

00:00:11.503 --> 00:00:13.005
A cup of tea.

00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:16.468
Yes, dear.

00:00:16.528 --> 00:00:19.391
Here you are.

00:00:19.411 --> 00:00:21.454
Yes, dear.

00:00:21.514 --> 00:00:22.955
Here you are.

00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:24.877
Yes, dear.

00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:28.658
Oh.

00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:33.759
Would you like some jam, mother?

00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:36.231
I don't like ham, Nancy.

00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:37.933
You know I don't eat meat.

00:00:37.993 --> 00:00:39.915
I said jam, mother.

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:40.726
Not ham.

00:00:40.746 --> 00:00:43.418
Would you like some jam, mother?

00:00:43.478 --> 00:00:45.360
Yes, please, Nancy.

00:00:45.421 --> 00:00:47.462
I hope it's strawberry jam.

00:00:47.522 --> 00:00:49.254
I like strawberry jam.

00:00:49.314 --> 00:00:53.098
I don't like raspberry jam, and I don't like plum jam.

00:00:53.158 --> 00:00:54.129
And I don't like this.

00:00:54.189 --> 00:00:55.820
Yes, I know, Mother.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.222
I only buy strawberry jam.

00:00:58.282 --> 00:01:02.765
Yes, strawberry jam for the last five years, just for her.

00:01:02.805 --> 00:01:04.406
Not again.

00:01:04.446 --> 00:01:06.958
There are other people in this family, dear.

00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:09.270
I like raspberry jam.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.302
You can do the shopping next week and then you buy what you want.

00:01:13.362 --> 00:01:15.584
You know I have no time.

00:01:15.644 --> 00:01:17.369
No, dear.

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:20.564
I don't like strawberry jam all the time.

00:01:20.605 --> 00:01:22.606
Not again, eat.

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:26.858
We're going on a nice family seaside holiday for a week.

00:01:26.918 --> 00:01:33.022
You can have raspberry jam for breakfast in the hotel and mum can have strawberry jam, okay?

00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:35.023
Yes dear.

00:01:35.082 --> 00:01:38.885
Oh, here you are Boris.

00:01:38.945 --> 00:01:42.589
Have my jam sandwich.

00:01:42.648 --> 00:01:46.442
Don't give Boris your sandwich.

00:01:46.502 --> 00:01:48.243
You know what happens.

00:01:48.303 --> 00:01:49.804
He looks hungry.

00:01:49.824 --> 00:01:52.565
I don't think you give him enough food.

00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:54.356
It's not a horse, Mum.

00:01:54.416 --> 00:01:56.207
It's not a real dog.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:59.639
A real dog is a golden retriever.

00:01:59.699 --> 00:02:01.960
I like golden retrievers.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.592
Boris is noisy and smelly.

00:02:04.612 --> 00:02:06.363
That reminds me.

00:02:06.422 --> 00:02:08.994
Why are we taking your mother on holiday?

00:02:09.014 --> 00:02:11.015
You know what happened last year.

00:02:11.075 --> 00:02:12.616
Not again, Pete.

00:02:12.676 --> 00:02:15.167
We can't leave her alone in the house.

00:02:15.227 --> 00:02:16.558
Why not?

00:02:16.618 --> 00:02:18.559
What's he saying about me?

00:02:18.579 --> 00:02:20.680
I know he's talking about me.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.752
I know he's talking about me.

00:02:22.812 --> 00:02:24.002
He doesn't like me.

00:02:24.022 --> 00:02:25.193
No, Mother.

00:02:25.253 --> 00:02:26.464
It's OK.

00:02:26.524 --> 00:02:29.536
He's talking about the lovely holiday together.

00:02:29.596 --> 00:02:30.616
No, he's not.

00:02:30.676 --> 00:02:31.637
Yes, he is.

00:02:31.697 --> 00:02:32.757
No, I'm not.

00:02:32.817 --> 00:02:33.858
No, he's not.

00:02:33.918 --> 00:02:35.349
Yes, he is.

00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:37.650
I'll stop this, everyone.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:41.464
I want a nice relaxing breakfast please.

00:02:41.524 --> 00:02:43.476
We have a long journey today.

00:02:43.536 --> 00:02:49.164
Please try to be nice to each other for one minute.

00:02:49.224 --> 00:02:53.130
Not again.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.531
I can't believe it.

00:02:54.551 --> 00:02:55.651
Stop that, Josephine.

00:02:55.691 --> 00:02:57.712
It's not nice at the breakfast table.

00:02:57.772 --> 00:02:58.742
Why not?

00:02:58.802 --> 00:03:00.002
Because I say so.

00:03:00.062 --> 00:03:02.823
I tell you every morning not to do that.

00:03:02.883 --> 00:03:04.294
I want to.

00:03:04.354 --> 00:03:05.894
Robbie's hungry.

00:03:05.954 --> 00:03:08.265
You can feed it in your room in its cage.

00:03:08.325 --> 00:03:10.475
Please keep it in its cage.

00:03:10.515 --> 00:03:12.386
You get lonely.

00:03:12.446 --> 00:03:15.017
I don't know why she has a pet rat.

00:03:15.077 --> 00:03:16.047
It's unhealthy.

00:03:16.107 --> 00:03:18.128
We said Josephine can have a pet.

00:03:18.188 --> 00:03:19.308
Don't you remember?

00:03:19.368 --> 00:03:24.840
Of course I remember, but a cat or a dog, not a parasite.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.171
I like Robbie.

00:03:26.231 --> 00:03:27.301
He's sweet.

00:03:27.361 --> 00:03:28.302
It smells.

00:03:28.362 --> 00:03:29.292
No, it doesn't.

00:03:29.352 --> 00:03:30.382
Yes, it does.

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:31.733
I like Robbie.

00:03:31.793 --> 00:03:32.733
He's sweet.

00:03:32.793 --> 00:03:35.154
The rat is not coming on holiday.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:35.955
Why not?

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.056
Because it's not.

00:03:38.116 --> 00:03:40.326
Nancy, speak to your daughter, please.

00:03:40.366 --> 00:03:42.389
Why is it always me?

00:03:42.449 --> 00:03:44.142
No, Josephine.

00:03:44.201 --> 00:03:45.242
It's not coming.

00:03:45.302 --> 00:03:46.873
It can't stay in the hotel.

00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:49.124
But I like Robbie.

00:03:49.184 --> 00:03:49.935
He's sweet.

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:52.226
Be quiet, Mother.

00:03:52.286 --> 00:03:55.698
After breakfast, take it to your friend.

00:03:55.758 --> 00:03:57.209
She can look after it.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.920
But she's going out.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.101
Just do as I say, Josephine.

00:04:01.161 --> 00:04:02.432
Don't argue.

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:03.502
I like him.

00:04:03.522 --> 00:04:05.123
He's sweet.

00:04:05.183 --> 00:04:06.884
Thank you, Grand.

00:04:06.944 --> 00:04:08.354
You see?

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.650
Grand thinks Robbie is sweet.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.764
Maybe because it looks like her.

00:04:12.824 --> 00:04:15.185
Please, talking about me again.

00:04:15.245 --> 00:04:17.186
What did he say, Nancy?

00:04:17.246 --> 00:04:19.257
It's not good for my heart.

00:04:19.317 --> 00:04:21.498
He knows I have high blood pressure.

00:04:21.558 --> 00:04:22.798
I said that it looks.

00:04:22.838 --> 00:04:24.369
Not again, Pete.

00:04:24.429 --> 00:04:28.601
The rat is not coming with us.

00:04:28.641 --> 00:04:30.962
You hurt your mother, Josephine.

00:04:31.022 --> 00:04:32.142
I like him.

00:04:32.202 --> 00:04:33.243
It's sweet.

00:04:33.303 --> 00:04:37.106
I am getting very, very angry.

00:04:37.166 --> 00:04:40.349
Find me in the garage cleaning the car.

00:04:40.409 --> 00:04:47.124
It is the only place in this house where I can find some peace and quiet.

00:04:47.184 --> 00:04:51.238
Why did you marry him, Nancy?

00:04:51.278 --> 00:04:53.130
Not again, Mum.

00:04:53.189 --> 00:04:55.461
I liked Jonathan.

00:04:55.521 --> 00:04:57.743
You know he lived next door.

00:04:57.803 --> 00:05:00.005
He liked you too.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:02.376
He had very nice tea.

00:05:02.436 --> 00:05:04.948
He went to university.

00:05:05.008 --> 00:05:06.648
He's a doctor.

00:05:06.708 --> 00:05:08.268
Lovely house.

00:05:08.328 --> 00:05:10.519
I met his mother last week.

00:05:10.579 --> 00:05:17.452
He's not again mum.

00:05:17.512 --> 00:05:24.735
Go in your own room Josie and pack your suitcase.

00:05:24.795 --> 00:05:26.756
I want to pack my bag now.

00:05:26.816 --> 00:05:29.036
I don't want to go on holiday.

00:05:29.096 --> 00:05:30.835
It's math.

00:05:30.895 --> 00:05:33.646
The same totally naff town.

00:05:33.706 --> 00:05:35.568
The same naff hotel.

00:05:35.628 --> 00:05:36.759
The same naff food.

00:05:36.779 --> 00:05:38.412
That's enough, Josephine.

00:05:38.472 --> 00:05:40.003
You are coming with the family.

00:05:40.023 --> 00:05:42.737
You're too young to stay at home alone.

00:05:42.796 --> 00:05:46.361
Why don't we go to Spain or Mallorca?

00:05:46.421 --> 00:05:49.008
All my friends go abroad.

00:05:49.068 --> 00:05:52.846
Why do we always go to bloody, stupid blackpool?

00:05:52.906 --> 00:05:54.166
I hate it!

00:05:54.226 --> 00:05:58.878
I want to go to somewhere where I can chill out and meet some fit guys.

00:05:58.938 --> 00:06:01.059
Blackpool is nice!

00:06:01.119 --> 00:06:07.332
We can sit on the beach, we can go to the fair, we can ride on a donkey, we can have a...

00:06:07.352 --> 00:06:09.483
God, I'm a sodding donkey!

00:06:09.543 --> 00:06:12.724
Mum, I am 15 years old.

00:06:12.784 --> 00:06:16.190
I don't want to ride on a naffing donkey.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.486
I want to go to discos.

00:06:18.546 --> 00:06:20.077
Meet people.

00:06:20.137 --> 00:06:21.458
Have fun.

00:06:21.518 --> 00:06:22.098
No.

00:06:22.158 --> 00:06:23.599
This year it is blackpool.

00:06:23.659 --> 00:06:24.700
That is final.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.961
No more arguments and stop using those terrible words.

00:06:28.021 --> 00:06:29.522
I say what I want.

00:06:29.582 --> 00:06:31.873
But why do we always go to blackpool?

00:06:31.933 --> 00:06:33.384
Because...

00:06:33.444 --> 00:06:35.816
Because...

00:06:35.876 --> 00:06:38.791
Because we do.

00:06:38.851 --> 00:06:41.045
Don't take that dress mum.

00:06:41.085 --> 00:06:42.166
It's too short.

00:06:42.226 --> 00:06:43.396
I don't think it is.

00:06:43.456 --> 00:06:44.836
Yes, he is.

00:06:44.896 --> 00:06:47.417
Everyone can see your fat legs.

00:06:47.477 --> 00:06:49.358
I'm taking it.

00:06:49.417 --> 00:06:51.418
What's this?

00:06:51.478 --> 00:06:53.789
Why are you taking this?

00:06:53.849 --> 00:06:55.969
You never wear this for Dad.

00:06:56.029 --> 00:06:56.940
Is it new?

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.310
Give it to me, Josephine.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.040
I bought it for the holiday.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.453
Does Dad know you bought it?

00:07:02.513 --> 00:07:04.316
Dad, Dad, come here!

00:07:04.336 --> 00:07:05.407
Stop it, Josephine!

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:07.458
No, I didn't tell your father.

00:07:07.518 --> 00:07:10.360
It's a surprise.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.001
Why did you buy it?

00:07:12.061 --> 00:07:14.723
It looks very expensive.

00:07:14.783 --> 00:07:18.138
You are much too old to wear it.

00:07:18.198 --> 00:07:19.642
I know.

00:07:19.702 --> 00:07:23.574
It's that slimy Italian manager at the hotel.

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:25.076
What's his name?

00:07:25.136 --> 00:07:28.428
I know, um, squeegee or something.

00:07:28.488 --> 00:07:30.419
I don't know what you're talking about, Josephine.

00:07:30.479 --> 00:07:31.460
Yes, you do.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:34.722
The Italian manager, we meet every year.

00:07:34.742 --> 00:07:37.584
Oh, yes.

00:07:37.644 --> 00:07:40.566
Um, his name is not squeegee.

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:42.678
It's Luigi.

00:07:42.738 --> 00:07:45.696
Luigi Bertolini.

00:07:45.756 --> 00:07:47.622
And he's not slimy.

00:07:47.682 --> 00:07:49.643
He has charming and kind.

00:07:49.703 --> 00:07:51.204
I don't like him.

00:07:51.263 --> 00:07:54.965
He's got a spot, and he smells like a perfume factory.

00:07:55.025 --> 00:07:57.526
More thick holes, not spots.

00:07:57.585 --> 00:08:00.686
Did you do it with him last year, Mum?

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:02.757
No, I didn't.

00:08:02.817 --> 00:08:05.228
What a thing to say.

00:08:05.288 --> 00:08:07.548
You know how much I love your father.

00:08:07.608 --> 00:08:09.809
Why do you say that, Josephine?

00:08:09.869 --> 00:08:11.150
No reason, Mum.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:12.616
No reason.

00:08:12.676 --> 00:08:16.725
It's just that I bought a new bikini for the holiday.

00:08:16.784 --> 00:08:18.236
What do you think?

00:08:18.296 --> 00:08:19.407
Oh!

00:08:19.466 --> 00:08:21.938
Oh no, mother!

00:08:21.998 --> 00:08:23.659
What's the matter?

00:08:23.719 --> 00:08:24.950
I like it.

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:26.781
Red is a nice colour.

00:08:26.841 --> 00:08:30.884
The woman in the shop said that red is the colour for this year.

00:08:30.944 --> 00:08:33.576
It's not the colour that's the problem.

00:08:33.636 --> 00:08:35.547
So what's the matter then?

00:08:35.607 --> 00:08:38.679
The problem is the bikini, Mother.

00:08:38.739 --> 00:08:41.621
It's, um, very small.

00:08:41.681 --> 00:08:44.814
Yes, I want to get a suntan this year.

00:08:44.874 --> 00:08:47.405
It's Blackpool, Mother, not the Caribbean.

00:08:47.425 --> 00:08:50.946
It rained last year and the year before.

00:08:51.006 --> 00:08:55.630
But don't you think you're a bit old for that bikini?

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:59.876
John at the Bingo Club said I have a good body.

00:08:59.936 --> 00:09:00.648
John?

00:09:00.708 --> 00:09:01.959
From across the road?

00:09:01.979 --> 00:09:03.761
It's totally blind.

00:09:03.781 --> 00:09:04.973
He has a white stick.

00:09:05.033 --> 00:09:05.994
Yes, I know.

00:09:06.054 --> 00:09:10.626
But he feels I have a great body.

00:09:10.685 --> 00:09:17.004
A cloudier shiffer has a red bikini just like this one.

00:09:17.064 --> 00:09:19.176
I saw it on television.

00:09:19.236 --> 00:09:22.797
Mother, you cannot wear that.

00:09:22.857 --> 00:09:25.988
It's super grand.

00:09:26.048 --> 00:09:28.469
Don't listen to Nancy.

00:09:28.529 --> 00:09:32.341
Oh please, wear it on the beach and tell me what happens.

00:09:32.401 --> 00:09:34.352
Don't say that, Josephine.

00:09:34.412 --> 00:09:36.542
She's too old to wear that.

00:09:36.602 --> 00:09:37.813
I like it.

00:09:37.873 --> 00:09:40.874
I hope the young men on the beach like it too.

00:09:40.934 --> 00:09:44.905
Oh dear Mother, you get worse as you get older.

00:09:44.965 --> 00:09:47.395
Please go and finish your packing.

00:09:47.435 --> 00:09:48.896
We're all ready late.

00:09:48.956 --> 00:09:51.136
Pete gets angry if we're late.

00:09:51.196 --> 00:09:53.046
Yes dear, yes dear.

00:09:53.106 --> 00:09:55.667
Just a few more things to pack.

00:09:55.727 --> 00:10:00.068
Oh, this tanger thing is a bit uncomfortable.

00:10:00.128 --> 00:10:02.798
Does it look alright from behind?

00:10:02.858 --> 00:10:04.129
No, it doesn't.

00:10:04.189 --> 00:10:05.349
Oh, it looks fun.

00:10:05.409 --> 00:10:07.590
Tast it, Grand.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:11.075
Go and ask Dad what he thinks.

00:10:11.135 --> 00:10:13.254
That's a good idea.

00:10:13.274 --> 00:10:15.099
He's a man.

00:10:15.159 --> 00:10:17.466
No, it's not a good idea, Mum.

00:10:17.526 --> 00:10:24.434
Josephine is joking.

00:10:24.494 --> 00:10:30.510
Heat.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:32.571
Come into the house please.

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:34.223
Our suitcase is ready.

00:10:34.243 --> 00:10:36.846
I think my mother is ready too.

00:10:36.906 --> 00:10:37.857
Okay.

00:10:37.917 --> 00:10:39.178
The car's ready.

00:10:39.238 --> 00:10:41.951
The engine sounds fantastic.

00:10:42.011 --> 00:10:46.892
No problems.

00:10:46.952 --> 00:10:51.673
I'm not too sure.

00:10:51.693 --> 00:10:54.336
It's another rip with a bag.

00:10:54.396 --> 00:10:55.216
Yes!

00:10:55.276 --> 00:10:57.709
So she is coming with us.

00:10:57.769 --> 00:10:59.740
Of course she is.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.044
Super terrific, fantastic.

00:11:03.104 --> 00:11:13.720
I am so...

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:24.044
Can I come in?

00:11:24.104 --> 00:11:25.235
Are you ready?

00:11:25.295 --> 00:11:26.756
I want to take your bag.

00:11:26.816 --> 00:11:28.968
You want to take me back?

00:11:29.028 --> 00:11:30.618
No, don't.

00:11:30.678 --> 00:11:32.559
I don't want to go back there.

00:11:32.619 --> 00:11:33.650
Not there.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:36.011
Nancy said I can stay here.

00:11:36.071 --> 00:11:36.982
What?

00:11:37.042 --> 00:11:38.212
What are you talking about?

00:11:38.272 --> 00:11:39.483
Nancy, stop him.

00:11:39.503 --> 00:11:40.884
He wants to take me back.

00:11:40.944 --> 00:11:42.665
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:11:42.725 --> 00:11:43.655
Let me stay.

00:11:43.715 --> 00:11:44.986
Don't send me back.

00:11:45.006 --> 00:11:46.557
Shut up, please.

00:11:46.617 --> 00:11:50.949
All I said was that I want to take your B-A-G bag.

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:52.060
BAG!

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:53.702
Problem now.

00:11:53.762 --> 00:11:55.695
Who wants to take me back?

00:11:55.754 --> 00:11:57.246
He doesn't like me.

00:11:57.306 --> 00:11:59.269
Why did you say that, Pete?

00:11:59.329 --> 00:12:01.902
Why don't you always upset my mother?

00:12:01.962 --> 00:12:05.898
All I said to the old fossil was that I want to take her back.

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:06.578
Bag!

00:12:06.638 --> 00:12:07.329
Bag!

00:12:07.389 --> 00:12:09.873
I am not an old fossil!

00:12:09.932 --> 00:12:15.197
Robert, a friend at the Bingo Club said, I'll look like Marilyn Monroe.

00:12:15.257 --> 00:12:17.448
Robert thinks everyone looks like her.

00:12:17.508 --> 00:12:19.680
Last week he called me, Marilyn.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.522
Stop it, both of you.

00:12:21.582 --> 00:12:25.665
Take her suitcase, Pete, and then collect Josie's.

00:12:25.725 --> 00:12:27.767
What is in this suitcase?

00:12:27.827 --> 00:12:29.338
It's so heavy.

00:12:29.398 --> 00:12:31.520
Are you stealing our silver?

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.721
Don't start again, Pete.

00:12:33.781 --> 00:12:38.092
I'm going, I'm going.

00:12:38.152 --> 00:12:41.861
It's too loud!

00:12:41.921 --> 00:12:45.453
Stop playing now, Josephine!

00:12:45.513 --> 00:12:46.884
Turn it down!

00:12:46.944 --> 00:12:48.454
What a noise!

00:12:48.514 --> 00:12:50.406
Stop playing!

00:12:50.466 --> 00:12:52.006
Can you say that?

00:12:52.066 --> 00:12:54.777
I said, turn it down!

00:12:54.838 --> 00:12:57.690
Oh, you have.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:00.941
Why do you play that terrible music, Josephine?

00:13:01.001 --> 00:13:02.472
I think it's great!

00:13:02.532 --> 00:13:05.053
It's what I want to do to write music.

00:13:05.113 --> 00:13:08.689
You think you can make a living with that kind of music?

00:13:08.749 --> 00:13:10.373
Well, I was young.

00:13:10.433 --> 00:13:12.784
They knew how to write music.

00:13:12.844 --> 00:13:14.825
And the words were important.

00:13:14.885 --> 00:13:15.705
And now...

00:13:15.765 --> 00:13:16.076
Yes, Dad.

00:13:16.136 --> 00:13:16.716
I know.

00:13:16.756 --> 00:13:18.126
You tell me every day.

00:13:18.186 --> 00:13:19.737
When you get older.

00:13:19.757 --> 00:13:19.997
Oh, yes.

00:13:20.037 --> 00:13:21.228
Same old story.

00:13:21.288 --> 00:13:22.568
Shut up.

00:13:22.628 --> 00:13:24.739
I'm not interested.

00:13:24.759 --> 00:13:27.640
I don't want any arguments on holiday.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.631
This is the only time your mother and I can relax.

00:13:30.691 --> 00:13:33.202
I don't want any problems, Josephine.

00:13:33.262 --> 00:13:36.874
Come with me and bring your suitcase to the car now.

00:13:36.934 --> 00:13:38.480
Nap, Blackpool.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:14:03.996
boring family boring life hate it hurry up Nancy get in the car we're waiting just wait a minute dear granny isn't here you don't want to go without her do you I said you don't want to go I hurt you No, I don't want to go without her.

00:14:04.056 --> 00:14:06.288
But perhaps we could try it.

00:14:06.348 --> 00:14:09.589
Be honest to a dear for once in your life.

00:14:09.649 --> 00:14:12.040
We're all the family she has now.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:13.261
Yes, dear.

00:14:13.321 --> 00:14:15.322
But where is she?

00:14:15.382 --> 00:14:17.093
Get off Boris!

00:14:17.153 --> 00:14:18.834
Stop it!

00:14:18.874 --> 00:14:20.615
Don't get Morris excited.

00:14:20.675 --> 00:14:23.176
You know what happens if he gets too excited.

00:14:23.196 --> 00:14:24.537
Stop it, Morris!

00:14:24.597 --> 00:14:25.818
Don't do that!

00:14:25.878 --> 00:14:26.898
Oh!

00:14:26.958 --> 00:14:28.589
No!

00:14:28.649 --> 00:14:30.169
What's wrong, Pete?

00:14:30.229 --> 00:14:33.100
What's that smell?

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:36.592
Why do we keep this dog dead off me?

00:14:36.652 --> 00:14:38.354
Look what he's done.

00:14:38.414 --> 00:14:40.346
Oh.

00:14:40.406 --> 00:14:42.468
Now I have to change my shirt.

00:14:42.528 --> 00:14:44.478
What a family.

00:14:44.538 --> 00:14:47.071
Wonderful start to the holiday.

00:14:47.131 --> 00:14:48.372
Why?

00:14:48.432 --> 00:14:50.013
Oh, what?

00:14:50.053 --> 00:14:52.765
Boris was sick on Dad's shirt.

00:14:52.825 --> 00:14:56.488
It's not fun.

00:14:56.548 --> 00:14:58.400
Boris, come here, sick quietly.

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:02.298
You're a bad dog.

00:15:02.358 --> 00:15:08.016
Oh, where's your husband Nancy?

00:15:08.036 --> 00:15:10.397
He's always late.

00:15:10.456 --> 00:15:12.937
Oh, what's that smell?

00:15:12.997 --> 00:15:14.177
Is it Pete?

00:15:14.237 --> 00:15:15.077
It smells?

00:15:15.117 --> 00:15:16.658
Yes mother, thank you.

00:15:16.678 --> 00:15:20.569
Boris was sick on Pete, he's changing his shirt.

00:15:20.629 --> 00:15:24.370
I don't know why you married him Nancy.

00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:26.427
What's that noise?

00:15:26.487 --> 00:15:30.236
You got that rat with you, Josephine.

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:34.150
Oh no, your father told you not to bring it.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:35.280
No, Mum.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:38.283
But I want Robbie to come on a holiday.

00:15:38.303 --> 00:15:40.734
He's very quiet.

00:15:40.794 --> 00:15:42.506
Please don't tell Dad.

00:15:42.566 --> 00:15:43.507
Please.

00:15:43.567 --> 00:15:44.688
I like him.

00:15:44.748 --> 00:15:45.969
He's sweet.

00:15:45.989 --> 00:15:47.099
Please, Mum.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.932
Promise not to say anything, please.

00:15:49.992 --> 00:15:52.344
I'm not happy Josephine.

00:15:52.404 --> 00:15:54.055
Your father said no.

00:15:54.075 --> 00:15:56.977
When he finds out that you have that rat with you.

00:15:56.997 --> 00:15:58.898
I hate pets.

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.814
Why do we keep it?

00:16:00.874 --> 00:16:02.368
I like him.

00:16:02.428 --> 00:16:03.609
He's sweet.

00:16:03.669 --> 00:16:06.660
It's loud and too expensive.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:09.112
I don't know what you mean.

00:16:09.172 --> 00:16:13.414
He's always very quiet and he costs nothing to feed.

00:16:13.474 --> 00:16:17.766
Josephine, show him what are you talking about, Gran.

00:16:17.826 --> 00:16:20.637
You gave it a jam sandwich at the breakfast table.

00:16:20.697 --> 00:16:23.289
I didn't feed him at the breakfast table.

00:16:23.349 --> 00:16:24.250
Yes, you did.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:25.170
I saw you.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:27.442
You fed it a strawberry sandwich.

00:16:27.502 --> 00:16:28.673
No, I didn't.

00:16:28.733 --> 00:16:30.644
Please tell him Nancy.

00:16:30.704 --> 00:16:32.486
Don't ask Nancy.

00:16:32.546 --> 00:16:34.827
I think your mother is losing her memory.

00:16:34.887 --> 00:16:38.670
Perhaps an old people's home is the place for her now.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.461
He doesn't like me, Nancy.

00:16:40.521 --> 00:16:43.003
He wants to put me into a home.

00:16:43.063 --> 00:16:45.155
I always knew he didn't like me.

00:16:45.215 --> 00:16:47.186
Both of you be quiet.

00:16:47.246 --> 00:16:49.757
I'm getting one of my headaches.

00:16:49.817 --> 00:16:54.089
I just want a few days of relaxation.

00:16:54.149 --> 00:16:57.291
Everyone be quiet.

00:16:57.350 --> 00:17:02.905
You can't wear that t-shirt, dear.

00:17:02.925 --> 00:17:06.537
It's too small and I can see you're stuck.

00:17:06.597 --> 00:17:08.158
It looks good.

00:17:08.218 --> 00:17:09.959
I always wear it on holiday.

00:17:10.019 --> 00:17:12.992
I know, dear, but it's very old.

00:17:13.052 --> 00:17:15.383
You have other new t-shirts.

00:17:15.443 --> 00:17:18.618
I know, but this is my favourite.

00:17:18.678 --> 00:17:23.706
Do you think a t-shirt with a picture of Cliff Richard on it is all right?

00:17:23.766 --> 00:17:27.169
We are staying at the Grand Park Hotel.

00:17:27.189 --> 00:17:30.292
I don't think it's a good idea.

00:17:30.352 --> 00:17:32.354
It's my holiday as well.

00:17:32.414 --> 00:17:34.066
I think it's great.

00:17:34.126 --> 00:17:36.198
I like Cliff Richard.

00:17:36.259 --> 00:17:38.200
He's a nice man.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:42.264
Why didn't you marry someone like Cliff Richard Nancy?

00:17:42.324 --> 00:17:46.227
He's got a lovely smile, a lovely tea.

00:17:46.287 --> 00:17:53.362
Ooh, a summer holiday, a summer holiday, summer holiday, summer holiday.

00:17:53.422 --> 00:17:54.532
Is this car okay?

00:17:54.592 --> 00:18:02.081
Of course, no problems.

00:18:02.141 --> 00:18:07.788
Are we ready now?

00:18:07.848 --> 00:18:08.619
Can we go?

00:18:08.679 --> 00:18:09.860
Wait a minute.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:12.072
I must go to the toilet again.

00:18:12.112 --> 00:18:14.904
Just wait a minute, please.

00:18:14.964 --> 00:18:17.906
Oh, no.

00:18:17.966 --> 00:18:21.679
I don't want to stop every ten minutes for your mother.

00:18:21.739 --> 00:18:25.432
Nancy, we have 250 miles to drive today.

00:18:25.492 --> 00:18:28.864
I hope this piece of junk can go 250 miles.

00:18:28.884 --> 00:18:31.306
No problem, trust me.

00:18:31.366 --> 00:18:34.688
Sometimes I think you don't trust me, dear.

00:18:34.748 --> 00:18:35.868
No.

00:18:35.928 --> 00:18:37.359
You're right.

00:18:37.419 --> 00:18:38.930
I don't trust you.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:45.202
I'm okay.

00:18:45.262 --> 00:18:59.782
We can go.

00:18:59.842 --> 00:19:17.696
Twelve hours to drive 250 miles.

00:19:17.756 --> 00:19:21.080
It's now nearly midnight.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:21.820
I'm hungry.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.432
I want a burger.

00:19:23.492 --> 00:19:26.434
Oh, that's a good idea Josie.

00:19:26.494 --> 00:19:28.156
I want one too.

00:19:28.216 --> 00:19:30.027
What a terrible journey.

00:19:30.087 --> 00:19:32.248
It was worse than last year.

00:19:32.308 --> 00:19:36.620
Yes, but this is the last holiday we come in that car.

00:19:36.681 --> 00:19:37.221
Yes.

00:19:37.281 --> 00:19:42.414
I am not coming to Blackpool again in a car that breaks down every 20 miles.

00:19:42.474 --> 00:19:43.804
I'm hungry.

00:19:43.864 --> 00:19:47.536
I want a burger with chips and lots of tomato ketchup.

00:19:47.596 --> 00:19:49.388
How are you trying to say Pete?

00:19:49.448 --> 00:19:52.706
Yes, but Nothing, dear.

00:19:52.766 --> 00:19:54.467
I want a new car.

00:19:54.527 --> 00:19:54.997
Yes.

00:19:55.057 --> 00:19:57.719
Or my friend's laugh when they see us in that car.

00:19:57.779 --> 00:19:59.370
It's quicker by bike.

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:01.212
And a new car.

00:20:01.272 --> 00:20:02.783
And no, a large one.

00:20:02.843 --> 00:20:04.224
I am on holiday.

00:20:04.284 --> 00:20:08.141
Yes, but it is a classic car.

00:20:08.201 --> 00:20:09.655
What's wrong with it?

00:20:09.716 --> 00:20:16.800
It is old, unreliable, uncomfortable, noisy, smelly, expensive.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.601
I hate the colour, I hate it!

00:20:19.661 --> 00:20:21.963
Do you understand?

00:20:22.023 --> 00:20:23.914
So, you don't like it dear?

00:20:23.974 --> 00:20:24.824
No!

00:20:24.884 --> 00:20:26.806
I don't like it!

00:20:26.826 --> 00:20:28.546
Do you ever listen to me?

00:20:28.606 --> 00:20:29.457
Sorry?

00:20:29.517 --> 00:20:33.191
I don't hungry, I want a burger.

00:20:33.211 --> 00:20:34.712
Be quiet, Josephy, not now.

00:20:34.732 --> 00:20:37.635
We can buy you a burger as well, Nancy.

00:20:37.695 --> 00:20:39.116
No, thank you, Mum.

00:20:39.176 --> 00:20:40.848
Burgers are not healthy.

00:20:40.908 --> 00:20:42.530
I'm on a diet.

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:44.752
You're always on a diet.

00:20:44.812 --> 00:20:47.250
You still look fat.

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:50.117
Come here Boris, come here.

00:20:50.177 --> 00:20:51.228
Don't do that.

00:20:51.288 --> 00:20:52.749
No, catch him.

00:20:52.809 --> 00:20:54.940
Why did you let him go?

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.551
I didn't let him go.

00:20:56.611 --> 00:20:58.572
He escaped through the car window.

00:20:58.632 --> 00:21:00.163
He's run onto the beach.

00:21:00.223 --> 00:21:02.775
I can hear him jumping in the waves.

00:21:02.835 --> 00:21:04.746
You can go and get him, Pete.

00:21:04.806 --> 00:21:05.587
Yes, dear.

00:21:05.647 --> 00:21:06.628
But why me?

00:21:06.688 --> 00:21:10.070
You are the name of the family, aren't you?

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:12.011
Sometimes I'm not so sure.

00:21:12.071 --> 00:21:13.651
What do you mean, Nancy?

00:21:13.711 --> 00:21:14.982
Nothing, dear.

00:21:15.042 --> 00:21:17.852
I suppose it happens when you get older.

00:21:17.872 --> 00:21:19.353
What happened?

00:21:19.413 --> 00:21:20.343
Nothing.

00:21:20.403 --> 00:21:23.213
Anyway, what about Boris?

00:21:23.274 --> 00:21:25.464
We can talk later.

00:21:25.524 --> 00:21:26.804
Josephine?

00:21:26.864 --> 00:21:27.514
Nancy?

00:21:27.574 --> 00:21:28.114
Grand?

00:21:28.174 --> 00:21:30.515
Can you come and help me?

00:21:30.575 --> 00:21:33.626
Thank you, everyone.

00:21:33.686 --> 00:21:35.428
Wonderful, all family.

00:21:35.488 --> 00:21:37.041
I'm hungry!

00:21:37.061 --> 00:21:39.293
I want a burger!

00:21:39.353 --> 00:21:42.006
With chips and lots of tomato ketchup.

00:21:42.066 --> 00:21:46.891
It's nearly midnight and all you two can think about is a burger.

00:21:46.911 --> 00:21:48.653
The burger shop is over there.

00:21:48.713 --> 00:21:49.624
I can see it.

00:21:49.684 --> 00:21:51.456
Five minutes and we're back.

00:21:51.516 --> 00:21:52.636
Come on, Gran.

00:21:52.696 --> 00:21:54.190
We're going.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:56.363
Have you got some money, Grand?

00:21:56.423 --> 00:22:01.465
Yes, but I want a double portion of chips and lots of tomato ketchup.

00:22:01.505 --> 00:22:04.765
No, Grand, if you're paying.

00:22:04.825 --> 00:22:06.806
You can have what you want.

00:22:06.866 --> 00:22:08.566
Choose a fiend.

00:22:08.626 --> 00:22:10.567
I want two burgers.

00:22:10.627 --> 00:22:11.667
I'm so hungry.

00:22:11.707 --> 00:22:13.107
I could eat Boris.

00:22:13.167 --> 00:22:14.328
One.

00:22:14.388 --> 00:22:17.698
Perhaps I can have a small burger as well.

00:22:17.759 --> 00:22:19.559
It is my holiday.

00:22:19.619 --> 00:22:21.850
One burger won't hurt my diet.

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:23.991
But I don't want any chips in the pension.

00:22:24.051 --> 00:22:25.832
Well done, Nancy.

00:22:25.892 --> 00:22:27.093
You only live once.

00:22:27.153 --> 00:22:29.464
It's about five minutes, Mum.

00:22:29.524 --> 00:22:30.584
Come on, Grant.

00:22:30.644 --> 00:22:32.135
Ooh, not so fast.

00:22:32.175 --> 00:22:34.936
You know I have a bad leg.

00:22:34.996 --> 00:22:37.758
It's Dad's birthday on Wednesday.

00:22:37.778 --> 00:22:40.500
Do you have a present for him?

00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:41.320
No.

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:42.310
Do you?

00:22:42.370 --> 00:22:42.881
No.

00:22:42.901 --> 00:22:45.742
I never know what to buy him.

00:22:45.802 --> 00:22:47.899
I can't be bothered.

00:22:47.959 --> 00:22:50.896
Mum always buys something for me to give him.

00:22:50.956 --> 00:22:52.856
It's easier.

00:22:52.916 --> 00:22:53.767
Dad doesn't know.

00:22:53.827 --> 00:22:56.058
Lancey does the same for me.

00:22:56.118 --> 00:22:59.659
I never know what to get your father either.

00:22:59.719 --> 00:23:02.950
Oh, but what can we do for him this year?

00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:05.541
Something a bit different.

00:23:05.601 --> 00:23:07.291
And a bit shocking.

00:23:07.351 --> 00:23:10.362
What about a new Cliff Richard T-shirt?

00:23:10.422 --> 00:23:11.933
Oh, it's naff.

00:23:11.993 --> 00:23:15.374
What about a stripper?

00:23:15.434 --> 00:23:17.909
Cool idea!

00:23:17.969 --> 00:23:21.103
But aren't they expensive?

00:23:21.163 --> 00:23:23.072
I wonder what mum thinks.

00:23:23.132 --> 00:23:24.833
Don't tell your mum.

00:23:24.893 --> 00:23:27.724
It's a surprise for both of them.

00:23:27.784 --> 00:23:30.825
Don't worry about the money I have enough with me.

00:23:30.885 --> 00:23:33.226
Oh, that's cool.

00:23:33.286 --> 00:23:35.366
What type of stripper?

00:23:35.426 --> 00:23:37.036
Leave it to me, Josie.

00:23:37.096 --> 00:23:38.087
Leave it to me.

00:23:38.147 --> 00:23:38.967
Oh, great.

00:23:39.027 --> 00:23:40.517
Well done, Grand.

00:23:40.577 --> 00:23:42.058
Oh, here we are.

00:23:42.118 --> 00:23:45.549
Now, don't forget, I want a double burger.

00:23:45.609 --> 00:23:49.420
No, a double cheese burger with extra chips.

00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:53.154
Oh, and do you think your dad wants a burger as well?

00:23:53.214 --> 00:23:54.815
Don't waste your money.

00:23:54.875 --> 00:23:59.070
Save it for the stripper.

00:23:59.130 --> 00:24:09.304
Anyway, I think he's too busy at the moment, chasing Boris through the waves.

00:24:09.364 --> 00:24:14.543
Where is that dog?

00:24:14.583 --> 00:24:15.884
I can't find him.

00:24:15.944 --> 00:24:19.325
We're not waiting in this car any longer, Pete.

00:24:19.385 --> 00:24:22.386
It's getting cold and I want my bed.

00:24:22.446 --> 00:24:23.896
So come on.

00:24:23.956 --> 00:24:26.057
Get the luggage and we can check in.

00:24:26.117 --> 00:24:27.077
OK.

00:24:27.137 --> 00:24:27.827
OK.

00:24:27.867 --> 00:24:30.248
I can look for him later, I suppose.

00:24:30.308 --> 00:24:31.948
What a day.

00:24:32.008 --> 00:24:33.959
You can look for him if you want.

00:24:34.019 --> 00:24:35.529
I'm tired.

00:24:35.590 --> 00:24:37.330
What's that smell?

00:24:37.390 --> 00:24:39.520
What are you eating, Josie?

00:24:39.580 --> 00:24:41.129
A burger.

00:24:41.189 --> 00:24:45.399
You too, Gran, and Nancy, you were all eating.

00:24:45.459 --> 00:24:46.930
Where is my burger?

00:24:46.990 --> 00:24:48.511
I'm so hungry.

00:24:48.571 --> 00:24:49.652
Oh, sorry.

00:24:49.712 --> 00:24:51.763
We forgot to get you one.

00:24:51.823 --> 00:24:54.264
You didn't say you wanted a burger.

00:24:54.325 --> 00:24:57.136
That's because I wasn't here.

00:24:57.156 --> 00:25:02.089
I was running up on down the beach in the dark, looking for that stupid dog.

00:25:02.149 --> 00:25:04.150
I fell over twice.

00:25:04.210 --> 00:25:06.442
The couples were very angry.

00:25:06.502 --> 00:25:07.782
It was embarrassing.

00:25:07.842 --> 00:25:11.254
They were, um...

00:25:11.314 --> 00:25:15.188
Oh, wait a minute.

00:25:15.248 --> 00:25:18.940
I have a biscuit at the bottom of my handbag.

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:21.452
Oh, yes, here it is.

00:25:21.512 --> 00:25:24.213
Oh, thank you very much.

00:25:24.274 --> 00:25:26.075
Nice of you to think of me.

00:25:26.135 --> 00:25:27.766
Oh, how wonderful.

00:25:27.826 --> 00:25:29.097
One biscuit.

00:25:29.157 --> 00:25:30.838
Not even a chocolate biscuit.

00:25:30.898 --> 00:25:34.120
Just a plain, boring, tasteless biscuit.

00:25:34.180 --> 00:25:37.312
I hope I can sleep tonight on such a full stomach.

00:25:37.372 --> 00:25:40.364
There's no need to be so sarcastic.

00:25:40.424 --> 00:25:41.534
Ah!

00:25:41.594 --> 00:25:43.905
That tastes terrible, what is it?

00:25:43.945 --> 00:25:45.516
Give it to me, Pete.

00:25:45.576 --> 00:25:47.777
Now, where are my glasses?

00:25:47.837 --> 00:25:49.467
Oh, I can't find them.

00:25:49.527 --> 00:25:52.408
What does it say on the packet, Nancy?

00:25:52.468 --> 00:25:55.720
Wonderful, woofy biscuits.

00:25:55.779 --> 00:25:57.580
It's a dog biscuit.

00:25:57.640 --> 00:26:00.251
A dog biscuit?

00:26:00.271 --> 00:26:02.248
I ate a dog biscuit.

00:26:02.308 --> 00:26:06.185
I think I need a doctor and suddenly feel real.

00:26:06.245 --> 00:26:11.428
Don't worry it's okay when you start barking I can ask for a doctor.

00:26:11.488 --> 00:26:19.524
Come on let's go into the hotel.

00:26:19.584 --> 00:26:27.591
Oh, good evening, Mr. and Mrs. Britain and family.

00:26:27.651 --> 00:26:30.662
Oh, hello, Mr. Bertolini.

00:26:30.722 --> 00:26:34.185
Luigi, lovely to see you again.

00:26:34.205 --> 00:26:35.586
How are you?

00:26:35.606 --> 00:26:38.298
I'm fine, and you?

00:26:38.358 --> 00:26:39.969
Oh, we're all fine.

00:26:40.029 --> 00:26:41.190
Thank you.

00:26:41.250 --> 00:26:45.012
So nice to be here in your lovely hotel.

00:26:45.072 --> 00:26:49.345
You are looking younger than last year, Nancy.

00:26:49.405 --> 00:26:50.415
Do you think so?

00:26:50.435 --> 00:26:53.744
Oh, thank you so much.

00:26:53.804 --> 00:27:00.456
I made a reservation for two double rooms with a bathroom for one week.

00:27:00.516 --> 00:27:02.268
But I don't understand.

00:27:02.328 --> 00:27:04.220
You are one week early?

00:27:04.279 --> 00:27:07.612
You have a booking from next Saturday, not today.

00:27:07.673 --> 00:27:09.675
No, that is wrong.

00:27:09.735 --> 00:27:13.303
I phoned two months ago and booked seven nights for this week.

00:27:13.363 --> 00:27:20.325
No, I'm sorry Mr. Britain, I answered the phone myself and I put it into the computer system immediately.

00:27:20.385 --> 00:27:23.488
Oh no, I can't believe it!

00:27:23.548 --> 00:27:24.980
They must do so at the stage.

00:27:25.040 --> 00:27:26.142
I hope so.

00:27:26.202 --> 00:27:29.234
I am not going home at this time.

00:27:29.294 --> 00:27:32.026
I'm sure it isn't a problem, is it?

00:27:32.086 --> 00:27:33.377
Eh, let me see.

00:27:33.397 --> 00:27:39.162
I am sorry, but we only have one spare room at the moment.

00:27:39.222 --> 00:27:41.214
We are almost fully booked tonight.

00:27:41.274 --> 00:27:42.845
We have a wedding party.

00:27:42.905 --> 00:27:43.976
That's okay.

00:27:44.036 --> 00:27:47.148
My wife and daughter and I can have the one room.

00:27:47.208 --> 00:27:51.122
My wife's mother can sleep on some chairs in a hotel bath.

00:27:51.182 --> 00:27:55.275
If she gets thirsty in the night, she can have a drink or two.

00:27:55.315 --> 00:27:57.347
Nice, I don't think, Graham.

00:27:57.407 --> 00:27:57.958
Make sure.

00:27:57.978 --> 00:27:59.570
Stop it, Peter.

00:27:59.630 --> 00:28:01.762
Mum is not sleeping in the bar.

00:28:01.822 --> 00:28:04.015
I am not sleeping in the bar.

00:28:04.075 --> 00:28:07.529
I have a bad back and my plumbing is not so good.

00:28:07.549 --> 00:28:09.852
He's only joking.

00:28:09.912 --> 00:28:11.484
There is a bed for you.

00:28:11.544 --> 00:28:14.026
Of course I was only joking.

00:28:14.086 --> 00:28:16.890
Maybe you have a cupboard somewhere in the cellar.

00:28:16.950 --> 00:28:19.891
Monk is in the room with Josie and myself.

00:28:19.951 --> 00:28:23.003
You, Pete, can find somewhere else to sleep.

00:28:23.063 --> 00:28:23.673
What?

00:28:23.733 --> 00:28:25.234
No, Pete.

00:28:25.294 --> 00:28:27.354
It was your job to book the hotel.

00:28:27.414 --> 00:28:30.626
I can't get you to do a simple job like that.

00:28:30.686 --> 00:28:34.118
You made the mistake, so it's your problem.

00:28:34.178 --> 00:28:35.508
Where do I go?

00:28:35.568 --> 00:28:37.039
You can find another hotel.

00:28:37.099 --> 00:28:38.159
You can sleep on the beach.

00:28:38.219 --> 00:28:40.150
You can sleep in your wonderful car.

00:28:40.210 --> 00:28:41.441
I don't care.

00:28:41.501 --> 00:28:42.772
Good night.

00:28:42.832 --> 00:28:44.562
Luigi.

00:28:44.622 --> 00:28:47.523
Can you take me to our room, please?

00:28:47.583 --> 00:28:49.573
Of course, Nancy.

00:28:49.633 --> 00:28:51.134
This way, please.

00:28:51.194 --> 00:28:53.164
It's a nice room.

00:28:53.224 --> 00:28:55.715
Very comfortable beds.

00:28:55.775 --> 00:28:58.886
That sounds very nice.

00:28:58.946 --> 00:29:00.486
Come this way, please.

00:29:00.546 --> 00:29:02.907
We are back, Josephine.

00:29:02.967 --> 00:29:03.797
Mum?

00:29:03.857 --> 00:29:05.058
Come on.

00:29:05.118 --> 00:29:06.548
Good night, Dad.

00:29:06.608 --> 00:29:08.198
Sleep well.

00:29:08.258 --> 00:29:17.140
Sweet dreams.

00:29:17.200 --> 00:29:25.951
I can't believe it.

00:29:26.011 --> 00:29:27.952
Where were you Boris?

00:29:28.012 --> 00:29:29.754
Come here.

00:29:29.814 --> 00:29:31.836
Be quiet.

00:29:31.896 --> 00:29:35.240
Don't wake up the guests of the hotel.

00:29:35.300 --> 00:29:37.582
Be quiet.

00:29:37.642 --> 00:29:38.652
Come on.

00:29:38.712 --> 00:29:43.856
Get in the car.

00:29:43.916 --> 00:29:46.559
Just lay down, dog.

00:29:46.619 --> 00:29:48.060
Be quiet.

00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:49.817
I don't believe it.

00:29:49.877 --> 00:29:54.255
The first night of the holiday and I'm sleeping in the car with you!

00:29:54.275 --> 00:29:57.108
Stop barking!

00:29:57.168 --> 00:30:01.441
Can we try to sleep now please Boris?

00:30:01.501 --> 00:30:05.854
I am very, very tired.

00:30:05.914 --> 00:30:08.556
What's that?

00:30:08.616 --> 00:30:09.678
Go away!

00:30:09.738 --> 00:30:11.739
Be quiet dog!

00:30:11.799 --> 00:30:14.704
I'm going mad.

00:30:14.764 --> 00:30:17.658
What?

00:30:17.718 --> 00:30:19.309
Oh, no.

00:30:19.370 --> 00:30:20.460
The police.

00:30:20.520 --> 00:30:21.501
What?

00:30:21.561 --> 00:30:24.464
Please open your window, sir.

00:30:24.524 --> 00:30:25.754
Yes, sir.

00:30:25.814 --> 00:30:28.927
Get all the Boris.

00:30:28.947 --> 00:30:32.490
No, Boris, not there.

00:30:32.550 --> 00:30:36.213
Open your window now, please, sir.

00:30:36.273 --> 00:30:39.135
Yes, officer.

00:30:39.155 --> 00:30:39.755
Wait a minute.

00:30:39.775 --> 00:30:41.726
What Boris?

00:30:41.787 --> 00:30:44.390
What is the problem, sir?

00:30:44.450 --> 00:30:46.151
Ah, nothing, Officer.

00:30:46.211 --> 00:30:52.246
I just have a problem with the dog, and why are you sleeping in the car, sir?

00:30:52.306 --> 00:30:54.347
It's a long story.

00:30:54.408 --> 00:30:55.779
Get on it, Boris!

00:30:55.839 --> 00:30:56.259
Ow!

00:30:56.319 --> 00:30:58.140
It worked!

00:30:58.200 --> 00:30:59.922
Well, Officer.

00:30:59.982 --> 00:31:01.353
Yes, sir?

00:31:01.413 --> 00:31:12.244
Well, I said my wife's mother could sleep in the bar because she likes a drink or two, and you have a drink as well, sir.

00:31:12.304 --> 00:31:14.128
No, why?

00:31:14.188 --> 00:31:17.209
You are a little confused, sir.

00:31:17.269 --> 00:31:18.589
No, officer.

00:31:18.649 --> 00:31:20.749
It's all very simple.

00:31:20.809 --> 00:31:23.930
So, what are you doing now, sir?

00:31:23.950 --> 00:31:29.551
Staying here in a car for tonight, and I'm looking for another room in the morning.

00:31:29.611 --> 00:31:31.892
You can't park here, sir.

00:31:31.952 --> 00:31:36.192
This is a private car park for hotel guests only.

00:31:36.252 --> 00:31:39.013
I am a guest at this hotel.

00:31:39.073 --> 00:31:39.883
Oh.

00:31:39.943 --> 00:31:45.186
That's why you're sleeping in the hotel car park, is it, sir?

00:31:45.246 --> 00:31:52.039
It does sound a little strange, officer, but there is a simple explanation.

00:31:52.099 --> 00:31:53.379
Yes, sir.

00:31:53.439 --> 00:31:55.510
Of course there is, sir.

00:31:55.570 --> 00:31:58.322
I can see you don't believe me.

00:31:58.382 --> 00:32:01.583
What makes you think that, sir?

00:32:01.643 --> 00:32:08.036
You have one minute to explain to me why you're in this car with a mad barking dog.

00:32:08.096 --> 00:32:12.266
Well, It all started when I booked the hotel.

00:32:12.326 --> 00:32:19.462
The Italian manager said I booked for next week, but I know I booked for this week.

00:32:19.522 --> 00:32:23.615
That's the problem with foreigners, they don't understand English.

00:32:23.675 --> 00:32:26.978
Even when you shout at them, they don't understand.

00:32:27.038 --> 00:32:29.875
Isn't this important for your story, sir?

00:32:29.935 --> 00:32:33.891
Well, yes and no.

00:32:33.951 --> 00:32:40.652
Anyway, I thought I could sleep with the two women in one room and the mother-in-law could sleep in the bar.

00:32:40.712 --> 00:32:41.933
That's enough, sir.

00:32:41.993 --> 00:32:44.833
Can you move your car, sir, now?

00:32:44.893 --> 00:32:46.764
But where to?

00:32:46.824 --> 00:32:49.274
Perhaps you could drive home, sir.

00:32:49.334 --> 00:32:52.135
That's 250 miles.

00:32:52.195 --> 00:32:56.538
Well, you can't stay here and you can't stay on the seafront.

00:32:56.598 --> 00:33:02.836
There's a car pop behind the shopping centre, but I think that's closed at this time of night.

00:33:02.896 --> 00:33:06.269
I'm sorry, officer, but I'm staying here.

00:33:06.329 --> 00:33:07.520
That's final.

00:33:07.580 --> 00:33:08.902
I am tired.

00:33:08.962 --> 00:33:10.493
The day was terrible.

00:33:10.513 --> 00:33:13.428
I am staying here.

00:33:13.488 --> 00:33:17.432
That is not a good decision, sir.

00:33:17.492 --> 00:33:18.773
Why not?

00:33:18.833 --> 00:33:27.567
I think the best idea is that you come to the police station and then we can have a chat and sort things out there.

00:33:27.587 --> 00:33:30.218
You can bring your beast with you as well, sir.

00:33:30.278 --> 00:33:33.710
You are joking, officer, aren't you?

00:33:33.770 --> 00:33:35.830
No, I'm not.

00:33:35.890 --> 00:33:37.231
Shut up!

00:33:37.291 --> 00:33:39.212
Are you talking to me, sir?

00:33:39.272 --> 00:33:41.902
No, of course not.

00:33:41.962 --> 00:33:43.951
I'm on, sir.

00:33:44.011 --> 00:33:45.722
My core is over there.

00:33:45.782 --> 00:33:47.164
You can't do this.

00:33:47.224 --> 00:33:48.795
I am not a criminal.

00:33:48.815 --> 00:33:50.958
I can't believe it.

00:33:51.018 --> 00:33:53.130
It's your fault, Boris.

00:33:53.190 --> 00:33:54.822
A holiday.

00:33:54.882 --> 00:34:04.704
What a life.

00:34:04.764 --> 00:34:15.267
I wonder where Peter's at the moment.

00:34:15.327 --> 00:34:16.898
I hope he's okay.

00:34:16.958 --> 00:34:19.348
Don't worry about him, Nancy.

00:34:19.408 --> 00:34:21.689
I'm sure he has a bed somewhere.

00:34:21.749 --> 00:34:24.910
I think I was a bit unkind to him this evening.

00:34:24.970 --> 00:34:27.451
Don't worry so much.

00:34:27.512 --> 00:34:30.342
I think I ate too many burgers.

00:34:30.403 --> 00:34:32.113
I feel a bit strange.

00:34:32.173 --> 00:34:34.434
And you ate two ice creams?

00:34:34.494 --> 00:34:35.594
Yes, I know.

00:34:35.654 --> 00:34:41.106
I never eat ice cream at home, but this is my holiday.

00:34:41.167 --> 00:34:47.119
I want to phone Pete to see if he's okay.

00:34:47.179 --> 00:34:48.860
Where's my mobile, Josie?

00:34:48.880 --> 00:34:50.200
I don't know.

00:34:50.220 --> 00:34:52.161
Why ask me?

00:34:52.221 --> 00:34:54.511
You're always losing it.

00:34:54.571 --> 00:34:57.451
Oh no, I forgot about the rat.

00:34:57.511 --> 00:35:00.062
If your dad finds out, it's here with us.

00:35:00.122 --> 00:35:01.663
He won't find out.

00:35:01.723 --> 00:35:02.833
Don't tell him.

00:35:02.893 --> 00:35:04.724
It's not my problem, Josephine.

00:35:04.784 --> 00:35:06.465
You promised not to tell him.

00:35:06.485 --> 00:35:07.485
No, I didn't.

00:35:07.545 --> 00:35:09.216
Don't say anything, Mum.

00:35:09.276 --> 00:35:10.996
That's enough, Josephine.

00:35:11.056 --> 00:35:14.870
But it is not sleeping in the same room as us.

00:35:14.930 --> 00:35:17.284
Robbie's very quiet.

00:35:17.344 --> 00:35:18.706
He's no problem.

00:35:18.766 --> 00:35:20.468
Just chill out a bit, mum.

00:35:20.528 --> 00:35:23.022
It's not staying in the bedroom.

00:35:23.082 --> 00:35:25.024
Put it on the balcony, Josephine.

00:35:25.084 --> 00:35:27.676
I can't sleep with it in the room.

00:35:27.736 --> 00:35:30.090
Bloody marvellous.

00:35:30.150 --> 00:35:32.499
Where is my mobile?

00:35:32.559 --> 00:35:34.517
Mum, do you know where it is?

00:35:34.577 --> 00:35:35.678
What, Nancy?

00:35:35.738 --> 00:35:37.908
Robbie is in Josie's pocket.

00:35:37.928 --> 00:35:39.958
No, no, my mobile.

00:35:40.018 --> 00:35:41.039
Mobile what?

00:35:41.099 --> 00:35:44.609
Telephone, mobile phone, you know.

00:35:44.629 --> 00:35:46.700
The small telephone I have.

00:35:46.760 --> 00:35:49.440
There's a telephone by the side of the bed.

00:35:49.500 --> 00:35:53.981
No, I can't use that because I don't know where Pete is staying.

00:35:54.041 --> 00:35:55.852
With my mobile...

00:35:55.872 --> 00:35:57.682
Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:35:57.742 --> 00:36:00.382
Josie, I think it's in the car.

00:36:00.442 --> 00:36:03.103
Can you go down to the car, Park and have a look?

00:36:03.164 --> 00:36:04.184
Mom!

00:36:04.244 --> 00:36:05.235
Why me?

00:36:05.255 --> 00:36:07.308
Just do it, Josie, please.

00:36:07.368 --> 00:36:10.400
But Mom, I don't want to.

00:36:10.460 --> 00:36:11.481
You go.

00:36:11.501 --> 00:36:13.463
It's dark.

00:36:13.523 --> 00:36:15.736
We can go together, Josie.

00:36:15.796 --> 00:36:16.656
Come on.

00:36:16.716 --> 00:36:20.610
I think a little fresh air might be good for my stomach.

00:36:20.670 --> 00:36:27.335
I can't feel too good at the moment.

00:36:27.396 --> 00:36:34.129
Mum is super stressed at the moment, Grand.

00:36:34.189 --> 00:36:36.219
She really gets on my nerves.

00:36:36.279 --> 00:36:37.820
Don't worry, Josie.

00:36:37.880 --> 00:36:41.310
I'm sure it's nothing serious, but you are right.

00:36:41.370 --> 00:36:46.032
She is stressed, and sometimes she does strange things.

00:36:46.092 --> 00:36:48.522
Come here, you little thing.

00:36:48.582 --> 00:36:49.192
Oh.

00:36:49.252 --> 00:36:52.303
You don't want to sleep on that balcony tonight, do you?

00:36:52.363 --> 00:36:55.604
Oh, Robbie can sleep in the car, in the car park.

00:36:55.664 --> 00:36:58.234
After breakfast, you can feed him.

00:36:58.294 --> 00:36:59.435
What do you think?

00:36:59.495 --> 00:37:00.954
Well...

00:37:01.014 --> 00:37:04.224
It's better than the balcony, I suppose.

00:37:04.284 --> 00:37:08.797
Okay.

00:37:08.858 --> 00:37:11.210
Where is our car?

00:37:11.270 --> 00:37:13.201
They all look the same to me.

00:37:13.261 --> 00:37:15.292
It's easy to find our car.

00:37:15.352 --> 00:37:18.775
It's the only one that looks like it escaped from a museum.

00:37:18.836 --> 00:37:21.368
Oh yes, there it is.

00:37:21.428 --> 00:37:23.518
The car's empty.

00:37:23.578 --> 00:37:29.110
I thought that perhaps Dad and Boris were cuddling up on the backseat together.

00:37:29.170 --> 00:37:32.412
Oh, we must be quiet.

00:37:32.472 --> 00:37:34.662
It's late.

00:37:34.723 --> 00:37:38.714
Now, what is it we're looking for?

00:37:38.774 --> 00:37:42.156
Something called a no-bile, whatever that is.

00:37:42.216 --> 00:37:44.301
It's a Moby Grand.

00:37:44.361 --> 00:37:46.356
Don't you know what a Moby is?

00:37:46.376 --> 00:37:47.366
Um...

00:37:47.426 --> 00:37:48.306
Grand?

00:37:48.366 --> 00:37:49.127
Er...

00:37:49.187 --> 00:37:50.527
A mobile?

00:37:50.587 --> 00:37:52.158
Everyone has one?

00:37:52.218 --> 00:37:55.689
Oh, I don't understand this modern technology.

00:37:55.749 --> 00:37:59.500
I liked it when people talked to each other and wrote letters.

00:37:59.560 --> 00:37:59.871
Oh!

00:37:59.931 --> 00:38:01.431
You sound so old.

00:38:01.491 --> 00:38:02.092
Oh!

00:38:02.152 --> 00:38:04.745
Where is the Moby?

00:38:04.805 --> 00:38:07.459
I can't find it.

00:38:07.519 --> 00:38:08.999
It's not bloody here.

00:38:09.059 --> 00:38:09.919
Oh dear.

00:38:09.979 --> 00:38:11.020
Come on.

00:38:11.080 --> 00:38:12.700
Stupid mother.

00:38:12.760 --> 00:38:14.270
It must be in the bedroom.

00:38:14.330 --> 00:38:17.121
Don't forget to leave your little friend here.

00:38:17.181 --> 00:38:18.271
Oh yes.

00:38:18.331 --> 00:38:20.012
Come on Robbie.

00:38:20.072 --> 00:38:22.572
You can sleep here on this coat.

00:38:22.632 --> 00:38:23.803
Okay.

00:38:23.863 --> 00:38:26.283
Sleep well.

00:38:26.343 --> 00:38:31.084
I'm sleeping by myself on the sofa in the bedroom.

00:38:31.144 --> 00:38:33.354
You and Mum can have the double bed, OK?

00:38:33.414 --> 00:38:34.925
That's fine.

00:38:34.985 --> 00:38:36.795
I have a bad bed.

00:38:36.855 --> 00:38:37.555
Yes, I know.

00:38:37.575 --> 00:38:41.446
I wonder which hotel Dad is sleeping in.

00:38:41.506 --> 00:38:43.717
Maybe he's not alone.

00:38:43.777 --> 00:38:45.837
He's got Boris with him.

00:38:45.897 --> 00:38:50.018
Oh, yes, I forgot.

00:38:50.078 --> 00:38:53.439
I don't have a key for the bedroom, do you, Josie?

00:38:53.499 --> 00:38:57.332
No, but Mum is there, so don't get stressed.

00:38:57.392 --> 00:38:59.254
Try it again.

00:38:59.314 --> 00:39:02.576
Perhaps Nancy is in the bathroom.

00:39:02.636 --> 00:39:05.186
Strange.

00:39:05.246 --> 00:39:08.828
Mom, are you there?

00:39:08.888 --> 00:39:11.100
Open the sodding door.

00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:12.650
Is it the right room?

00:39:12.710 --> 00:39:14.742
They all look the same to me.

00:39:14.802 --> 00:39:16.662
Of course it's the right room.

00:39:16.722 --> 00:39:18.884
Mom, wake up.

00:39:18.944 --> 00:39:20.384
Open the bleeding door.

00:39:20.444 --> 00:39:23.126
Let us in.

00:39:23.186 --> 00:39:30.769
Oh, sorry, I, um, just, well, I went out for a minute.

00:39:30.829 --> 00:39:33.590
And you're quicker than I am.

00:39:33.650 --> 00:39:37.932
I was way longer than, er, er, you're all right, Nancy.

00:39:37.992 --> 00:39:40.174
You look a little hot and red.

00:39:40.234 --> 00:39:41.134
Were you running?

00:39:41.194 --> 00:39:43.486
No, er, yes, yes.

00:39:43.546 --> 00:39:45.616
I went for a jog in the hotel.

00:39:45.676 --> 00:39:48.018
I think it was the burger, too.

00:39:48.078 --> 00:39:52.584
I don't think a night dress is the right thing to wear for jogging, is it?

00:39:52.645 --> 00:39:55.038
It's very quiet in the hotel.

00:39:55.098 --> 00:39:57.272
No one saw us at Ernie.

00:39:57.332 --> 00:39:59.094
I can't find your Moby.

00:39:59.154 --> 00:40:00.506
I think it's lost.

00:40:00.566 --> 00:40:01.568
What's lost?

00:40:01.628 --> 00:40:03.335
Your mobile mum.

00:40:03.395 --> 00:40:05.000
My mobile?

00:40:05.060 --> 00:40:06.312
Oh, yes!

00:40:06.372 --> 00:40:07.933
How can I have it, please?

00:40:07.993 --> 00:40:09.844
I can't find it!

00:40:09.904 --> 00:40:11.125
I just told you!

00:40:11.145 --> 00:40:11.906
Okay.

00:40:11.966 --> 00:40:13.337
Right.

00:40:13.397 --> 00:40:14.438
Good.

00:40:14.498 --> 00:40:18.220
I think a good night's sleep is what we all need.

00:40:18.280 --> 00:40:19.661
Come on, Nancy.

00:40:19.722 --> 00:40:20.922
Open up the door.

00:40:20.982 --> 00:40:23.524
We don't have to stand in the corridor.

00:40:23.584 --> 00:40:24.975
Good idea, Mum.

00:40:24.995 --> 00:40:29.429
I'm in the bathroom first.

00:40:29.489 --> 00:40:32.622
Don't take too long, Josephine.

00:40:32.642 --> 00:40:41.815
What are you doing, Mom?

00:40:41.876 --> 00:40:46.364
I want to get my body in good shape.

00:40:46.404 --> 00:40:47.806
What is that?

00:40:47.866 --> 00:40:49.827
My fitness equipment.

00:40:49.887 --> 00:40:51.819
I brought it with me a muscle.

00:40:51.879 --> 00:40:53.250
It looks so good.

00:40:53.270 --> 00:40:55.672
This helps strengthen the lower muscles.

00:40:55.732 --> 00:41:04.888
I want to look good in my new string bikini.

00:41:04.948 --> 00:41:12.918
past 10 in the morning.

00:41:12.978 --> 00:41:14.643
Where is Pete?

00:41:14.703 --> 00:41:16.588
Where is my bikini?

00:41:16.649 --> 00:41:18.762
I can't find my sun cream mum.

00:41:18.822 --> 00:41:20.221
Where the hell is it?

00:41:20.281 --> 00:41:21.262
I don't know.

00:41:21.282 --> 00:41:23.493
Where is Pete?

00:41:23.553 --> 00:41:24.944
Why isn't he here?

00:41:24.964 --> 00:41:27.056
I want to go to the beach.

00:41:27.116 --> 00:41:28.778
Why is he so late?

00:41:28.838 --> 00:41:30.679
Where's my mobile?

00:41:30.739 --> 00:41:31.810
Here it is.

00:41:31.870 --> 00:41:32.710
My mobile?

00:41:32.770 --> 00:41:34.362
No, my bikini.

00:41:34.422 --> 00:41:36.463
Did you unpack the sun cream mum?

00:41:36.523 --> 00:41:38.885
Yes, it's in the bathroom, on the show.

00:41:38.945 --> 00:41:40.366
I'm ready for the beach.

00:41:40.426 --> 00:41:41.757
Come on, let's go.

00:41:41.817 --> 00:41:49.079
No, wait, I want to know where Pete is.

00:41:49.139 --> 00:41:56.208
Pete, why are you so late?

00:41:56.268 --> 00:41:58.399
It's half past ten.

00:41:58.459 --> 00:42:00.649
We had breakfast one hour ago.

00:42:00.709 --> 00:42:02.079
We're ready for the beach.

00:42:02.099 --> 00:42:03.630
The weather's lovely.

00:42:03.690 --> 00:42:04.990
Don't ask.

00:42:05.050 --> 00:42:06.901
Don't ask about my night.

00:42:06.961 --> 00:42:09.131
Did you find a nice hotel?

00:42:09.191 --> 00:42:12.272
Did I find a nice hotel?

00:42:12.332 --> 00:42:16.317
Yes, I do.

00:42:16.377 --> 00:42:20.274
Was the hotel nice?

00:42:20.334 --> 00:42:22.536
Oh yes, very nice.

00:42:22.596 --> 00:42:26.529
Single room, very warm, and breakfast in bed.

00:42:26.590 --> 00:42:27.640
Wonderful!

00:42:27.700 --> 00:42:29.763
And I didn't have to pay.

00:42:29.783 --> 00:42:31.454
What do you mean little after pay?

00:42:31.514 --> 00:42:33.166
I didn't have to pay.

00:42:33.226 --> 00:42:36.980
I stayed in a police station cell last night.

00:42:37.040 --> 00:42:37.910
What?

00:42:37.970 --> 00:42:39.802
You're joking, aren't you?

00:42:39.862 --> 00:42:40.342
No.

00:42:40.402 --> 00:42:41.913
I am not joking.

00:42:41.974 --> 00:42:45.334
Last night I was taken to the police station.

00:42:45.395 --> 00:42:54.777
After you threw me out of the hotel last night I tried to sleep in the car as it was so late, but Boris was barking and barking.

00:42:54.838 --> 00:43:00.679
Someone phoned the police and then this unfriendly policeman knocked on my car window and...

00:43:00.699 --> 00:43:02.470
How old was he?

00:43:02.530 --> 00:43:03.480
What?

00:43:03.540 --> 00:43:05.763
Why do you want to know how old he was?

00:43:05.823 --> 00:43:07.775
I like young policemen.

00:43:07.835 --> 00:43:10.506
It gives me goose pimples all over.

00:43:10.566 --> 00:43:12.557
Do you know his name?

00:43:12.617 --> 00:43:13.727
No, I don't.

00:43:13.787 --> 00:43:15.317
Where is Boris?

00:43:15.377 --> 00:43:16.287
What?

00:43:16.347 --> 00:43:17.218
Boris?

00:43:17.278 --> 00:43:18.658
He's in the car.

00:43:18.718 --> 00:43:20.618
I don't want to see him today.

00:43:20.678 --> 00:43:22.089
In the car?

00:43:22.149 --> 00:43:23.659
Oh, no.

00:43:23.719 --> 00:43:24.879
Did he see Rob...

00:43:24.939 --> 00:43:26.110
er...

00:43:26.150 --> 00:43:27.336
Mum's mobile.

00:43:27.397 --> 00:43:28.854
Mum's mobile.

00:43:28.914 --> 00:43:30.824
What are you talking about?

00:43:30.884 --> 00:43:35.446
I was in a police station last night and all you can ask about is Mum's mobile.

00:43:35.506 --> 00:43:37.127
I can't find it.

00:43:37.187 --> 00:43:38.487
Don't you understand?

00:43:38.507 --> 00:43:41.558
I am now a criminal.

00:43:41.618 --> 00:43:43.779
It's not so terrible, Pete.

00:43:43.839 --> 00:43:44.870
Yes, it is.

00:43:44.930 --> 00:43:47.191
I got a parking ticket last year.

00:43:47.251 --> 00:43:49.362
I left the car five minutes.

00:43:49.422 --> 00:43:51.886
A parking ticket?

00:43:51.946 --> 00:43:56.213
I slept in a police cell last night, Nancy.

00:43:56.273 --> 00:43:57.724
Don't you understand?

00:43:57.784 --> 00:43:59.678
I can't go anywhere now.

00:43:59.738 --> 00:44:02.631
Every policeman now has a photo of me.

00:44:02.651 --> 00:44:04.593
I can't leave the hotel.

00:44:04.653 --> 00:44:06.005
Don't be so stupid.

00:44:06.065 --> 00:44:07.366
You're here now.

00:44:07.426 --> 00:44:09.229
So come on and get ready.

00:44:09.289 --> 00:44:11.768
We want to start enjoying the holiday.

00:44:11.828 --> 00:44:13.696
Aren't you interested to know what happened?

00:44:13.756 --> 00:44:15.418
Must you go to prison?

00:44:15.478 --> 00:44:17.500
How many years?

00:44:17.560 --> 00:44:19.442
You can never come home again.

00:44:19.502 --> 00:44:22.674
I can make a cake for you with a file in it.

00:44:22.734 --> 00:44:24.286
No, ma'am.

00:44:24.346 --> 00:44:26.448
Pete doesn't have to go to prison.

00:44:26.468 --> 00:44:28.300
He can stay with us.

00:44:28.360 --> 00:44:30.813
That's good news, isn't it?

00:44:30.873 --> 00:44:35.008
I want to go to the beach in my new red bikini.

00:44:35.069 --> 00:44:37.041
Are you coming with me, Josephine?

00:44:37.101 --> 00:44:37.982
Nancy?

00:44:38.042 --> 00:44:39.494
Yes, I'm coming.

00:44:39.554 --> 00:44:42.880
I just want to look in the car for Rob.

00:44:42.940 --> 00:44:44.312
You're my bar, Mum.

00:44:44.372 --> 00:44:46.014
Thank you, Josie.

00:44:46.074 --> 00:44:48.048
I'm coming too, Mum.

00:44:48.108 --> 00:44:51.052
First I want to speak to Luigi.

00:44:51.112 --> 00:44:56.098
This morning at breakfast he said he now has two rooms for us for the rest of the week.

00:44:56.158 --> 00:44:59.051
I just want to say thank you.

00:44:59.111 --> 00:45:00.432
Just wait for me then.

00:45:00.492 --> 00:45:12.235
Give me two minutes to get ready.

00:45:12.295 --> 00:45:22.034
It's nice to see the sun and smell the fresh air.

00:45:22.094 --> 00:45:23.575
In prison, it was soon.

00:45:23.615 --> 00:45:24.715
We know, Pete.

00:45:24.756 --> 00:45:27.658
You told us the same story ten minutes ago.

00:45:27.718 --> 00:45:29.578
Don't you want to hear what happened to me?

00:45:29.638 --> 00:45:33.551
We're now lying on the beach and relaxing.

00:45:33.611 --> 00:45:36.373
Can we forget prisons and policemen?

00:45:36.433 --> 00:45:40.635
I can tell all my friends at school that my father is a criminal.

00:45:40.695 --> 00:45:42.466
No, you can't, Josephine.

00:45:42.526 --> 00:45:46.549
Did you see the prisoners on death row and the electric chair?

00:45:46.609 --> 00:45:48.688
You watched too many films.

00:45:48.748 --> 00:45:51.339
What is your mother wearing, Nancy?

00:45:51.399 --> 00:45:52.710
I can't believe it.

00:45:52.770 --> 00:45:55.142
Everyone on the beach is looking and laughing.

00:45:55.202 --> 00:45:56.633
Say something to her.

00:45:56.693 --> 00:46:00.056
I told her not to wear it, but she didn't listen.

00:46:00.116 --> 00:46:01.757
She looks like...

00:46:01.777 --> 00:46:02.978
She looks like...

00:46:03.038 --> 00:46:05.580
It's the bikini she's wearing.

00:46:05.640 --> 00:46:09.284
A bottom looks like two half-deflated hot air balloons.

00:46:09.344 --> 00:46:10.465
No, I can't look.

00:46:10.485 --> 00:46:11.415
Makes me feel ill.

00:46:11.476 --> 00:46:12.456
Look at the other way.

00:46:12.516 --> 00:46:14.416
It's difficult to look the other way.

00:46:14.476 --> 00:46:15.985
I know what you mean.

00:46:16.045 --> 00:46:19.406
Oh, there are some really thick guys on the beach.

00:46:19.466 --> 00:46:21.127
Really awesome.

00:46:21.187 --> 00:46:22.948
You all right, Josie?

00:46:23.008 --> 00:46:24.199
See you soon.

00:46:24.259 --> 00:46:25.639
Where are you going, mother?

00:46:25.699 --> 00:46:26.330
Excellent.

00:46:26.390 --> 00:46:27.590
Don't worry.

00:46:27.650 --> 00:46:29.871
What is your mother doing now?

00:46:29.932 --> 00:46:31.712
Why is she talking to him?

00:46:31.772 --> 00:46:33.874
Oh, he's real fit.

00:46:33.914 --> 00:46:34.884
Stop it, Josie.

00:46:34.944 --> 00:46:36.745
I don't know what she's doing.

00:46:36.805 --> 00:46:41.128
I really don't know.

00:46:41.188 --> 00:46:45.850
Excuse me, young man.

00:46:45.910 --> 00:46:49.171
It would be really nice if you could help me.

00:46:49.231 --> 00:46:50.811
What's the matter, dear?

00:46:50.871 --> 00:46:53.902
I'm not as young as I used to be, and I...

00:46:53.962 --> 00:46:55.263
No problem.

00:46:55.323 --> 00:46:56.593
What can I do for you?

00:46:56.653 --> 00:46:58.024
Put up your deck chair?

00:46:58.084 --> 00:46:58.794
No.

00:46:58.854 --> 00:46:59.954
Carry your bag?

00:47:00.014 --> 00:47:00.824
No.

00:47:00.884 --> 00:47:02.605
Just tell me what you want.

00:47:02.665 --> 00:47:03.956
Happy to help you.

00:47:04.016 --> 00:47:07.787
Can you rub some suntan oil over my body?

00:47:07.847 --> 00:47:09.246
What?

00:47:09.306 --> 00:47:14.618
Well, I'm very busy at the moment.

00:47:14.678 --> 00:47:17.710
I'm allergic to suntan oil.

00:47:17.770 --> 00:47:20.851
I think my wife is waving at me.

00:47:20.911 --> 00:47:21.751
I must go.

00:47:21.771 --> 00:47:22.732
Bye.

00:47:22.792 --> 00:47:25.242
Maybe tomorrow.

00:47:25.303 --> 00:47:26.873
I'm leaving.

00:47:26.933 --> 00:47:30.868
What a pity.

00:47:30.928 --> 00:47:34.864
Did you do, Mother?

00:47:34.924 --> 00:47:36.206
Why is he running away?

00:47:36.226 --> 00:47:38.368
I just asked him to help me.

00:47:38.428 --> 00:47:40.429
What did you ask him to do?

00:47:40.490 --> 00:47:41.972
Nothing much.

00:47:42.032 --> 00:47:48.478
Nancy, do you think I can take my bikini off to get an all over body turn?

00:47:48.538 --> 00:47:50.630
No, you cannot!

00:47:50.690 --> 00:47:53.142
I want an ice cream, Mum.

00:47:53.202 --> 00:47:54.946
I want some money.

00:47:55.006 --> 00:47:56.440
Here you are.

00:47:56.500 --> 00:47:59.121
Can you get us all an ice cream, Josie?

00:47:59.181 --> 00:48:00.561
You can choose.

00:48:00.621 --> 00:48:01.862
Okay.

00:48:01.922 --> 00:48:06.403
I can go and see if Boris is okay and look for...

00:48:06.463 --> 00:48:08.334
something.

00:48:08.394 --> 00:48:13.365
Your daughter is saying some very strange things these days, Nancy.

00:48:13.425 --> 00:48:15.335
She's your daughter as well.

00:48:15.395 --> 00:48:16.556
Yes.

00:48:16.616 --> 00:48:19.766
I suppose she is.

00:48:19.826 --> 00:48:22.837
Here you are.

00:48:22.897 --> 00:48:24.239
Ice cream for everyone.

00:48:24.259 --> 00:48:26.090
Thank you.

00:48:26.150 --> 00:48:29.244
Boris is unhappy in the car alone.

00:48:29.304 --> 00:48:32.207
The ice cream man was really buff.

00:48:32.267 --> 00:48:34.520
Great body.

00:48:34.580 --> 00:48:35.821
What does that mean?

00:48:35.881 --> 00:48:38.054
Oh, you're so old.

00:48:38.114 --> 00:48:38.954
Don't you know?

00:48:38.974 --> 00:48:40.416
When I was young.

00:48:40.436 --> 00:48:41.497
Oh yes, dad.

00:48:41.557 --> 00:48:42.792
Not again.

00:48:42.852 --> 00:48:44.815
Gave me his phone number.

00:48:44.876 --> 00:48:46.206
You are not meeting him.

00:48:46.266 --> 00:48:47.396
You are too young.

00:48:47.456 --> 00:48:48.697
Why not?

00:48:48.757 --> 00:48:50.187
That's not fair.

00:48:50.207 --> 00:48:52.418
He asked me for a drink.

00:48:52.478 --> 00:48:53.518
That's all.

00:48:53.578 --> 00:48:54.909
We can all come with you.

00:48:54.929 --> 00:48:56.000
What?

00:48:56.060 --> 00:48:57.830
Let her go by herself.

00:48:57.890 --> 00:48:59.041
Don't interfere.

00:48:59.101 --> 00:49:00.293
She's our daughter.

00:49:00.353 --> 00:49:03.546
I think it's okay for Josie to meet him.

00:49:03.606 --> 00:49:05.527
It's only for a drink.

00:49:05.587 --> 00:49:07.858
Don't you trust your daughter, Pete?

00:49:07.918 --> 00:49:09.499
She is too young.

00:49:09.559 --> 00:49:11.780
You know that he wants more than a drink.

00:49:11.840 --> 00:49:15.852
Is it the man on the promenade with long black hair, Josie?

00:49:15.912 --> 00:49:19.603
Yes, he smiled at me too when I walked past.

00:49:19.663 --> 00:49:22.575
I used to be attractive to men, Josie.

00:49:22.635 --> 00:49:23.985
Which century was that?

00:49:24.045 --> 00:49:26.536
The Middle Ages, before they invented the wheel.

00:49:26.596 --> 00:49:28.207
I want to meet him.

00:49:28.267 --> 00:49:30.303
I don't care what you say.

00:49:30.362 --> 00:49:31.548
You do as I tell you.

00:49:31.608 --> 00:49:32.858
Nancy speak to your daughter.

00:49:32.918 --> 00:49:34.239
Why ask me?

00:49:34.299 --> 00:49:35.910
You can speak to her yourself.

00:49:35.970 --> 00:49:38.361
I can go with Josie to meet him.

00:49:38.421 --> 00:49:39.782
Is that all right?

00:49:39.842 --> 00:49:41.383
Pete?

00:49:41.443 --> 00:49:43.624
I suppose so.

00:49:43.684 --> 00:49:45.405
But you know what your mother is like.

00:49:45.425 --> 00:49:47.646
She's very sensible.

00:49:47.666 --> 00:49:48.527
Hmm.

00:49:48.587 --> 00:49:50.098
I'm not so sure.

00:49:50.158 --> 00:49:51.509
Oh no.

00:49:51.569 --> 00:49:52.229
Look.

00:49:52.289 --> 00:49:53.880
It's getting cloudy.

00:49:53.940 --> 00:49:55.855
Where's the sun gone?

00:49:55.915 --> 00:49:57.721
Do you think it's going to rain?

00:49:57.781 --> 00:50:01.016
Typical bloody, nothing black or weather.

00:50:01.076 --> 00:50:02.598
Let's get in cold.

00:50:02.658 --> 00:50:04.582
Let's go back to the hotel.

00:50:04.642 --> 00:50:09.832
Mother, you can change out of that bikini and then we can go to the pleasure beach this afternoon.

00:50:09.892 --> 00:50:12.708
Can we go on the ghost train together?

00:50:12.768 --> 00:50:14.650
I want to sit at the front.

00:50:14.710 --> 00:50:16.813
And I want some candy floss.

00:50:16.873 --> 00:50:19.456
She gets more like a child each day.

00:50:19.516 --> 00:50:22.891
I really think we must go and see her doctor when we get home.

00:50:22.951 --> 00:50:25.134
Pete, please don't say that.

00:50:25.194 --> 00:50:28.507
Can we just try to have a nice day?

00:50:28.568 --> 00:50:29.908
Yes dear.

00:50:29.969 --> 00:50:31.610
Come on, everyone.

00:50:31.670 --> 00:50:33.382
Bring all our things.

00:50:33.442 --> 00:50:36.275
Hurry up, Josie.

00:50:36.335 --> 00:50:38.537
Mom, bring the towels and the sunshade.

00:50:38.577 --> 00:50:40.179
And don't forget your sunglasses.

00:50:40.219 --> 00:50:40.960
Yes, Mom.

00:50:40.980 --> 00:50:41.701
Yes, Mom.

00:50:41.721 --> 00:50:43.303
Don't go on all the time.

00:50:43.323 --> 00:50:45.375
Thanks, Grant.

00:50:45.436 --> 00:50:52.062
We can sort something out when we are alone.

00:50:52.122 --> 00:50:56.666
Oh!

00:50:56.726 --> 00:50:58.938
It's stuck to my nose!

00:50:58.998 --> 00:51:00.048
Help me, Nancy!

00:51:00.108 --> 00:51:00.809
Help me!

00:51:00.869 --> 00:51:02.400
It's OK, Grant!

00:51:02.440 --> 00:51:04.022
Let me help you!

00:51:04.082 --> 00:51:06.033
Candy Floss is such fun!

00:51:06.093 --> 00:51:07.204
I like it!

00:51:07.264 --> 00:51:09.726
It is so sweet and sticky!

00:51:09.746 --> 00:51:11.547
Oh, Pete!

00:51:11.608 --> 00:51:15.150
It's so good to see Mother enjoying herself!

00:51:15.210 --> 00:51:19.034
I hope Josephine looks after us when we're old.

00:51:19.094 --> 00:51:20.955
I'm not so sure, Nancy.

00:51:21.015 --> 00:51:22.766
It's a different generation.

00:51:22.826 --> 00:51:25.125
What do we do when we're old?

00:51:25.185 --> 00:51:26.382
I don't know.

00:51:26.442 --> 00:51:27.813
I don't know.

00:51:27.873 --> 00:51:30.604
Come on everyone to the ghost train.

00:51:30.664 --> 00:51:32.545
I'm coming with you, Grand.

00:51:32.605 --> 00:51:34.716
Mum and Dad are so naff.

00:51:34.776 --> 00:51:36.166
You do go.

00:51:36.226 --> 00:51:40.058
We want to sit in a cafe and have a quiet cup of tea.

00:51:40.118 --> 00:51:41.919
We can make here in a couple of hours.

00:51:41.979 --> 00:51:43.670
You're on holiday.

00:51:43.730 --> 00:51:44.560
Relax.

00:51:44.620 --> 00:51:45.610
I'm fun.

00:51:45.670 --> 00:51:49.442
Going on a ghost train is not my idea of fun.

00:51:49.502 --> 00:51:50.262
You go.

00:51:50.282 --> 00:51:52.224
Okay.

00:51:52.284 --> 00:51:54.156
Grand?

00:51:54.216 --> 00:51:55.920
Yes, Josie.

00:51:55.980 --> 00:51:58.144
Can I ask you a big favour?

00:51:58.204 --> 00:52:00.168
Of course, my dear.

00:52:00.228 --> 00:52:03.404
Please, don't tell mum and dad.

00:52:03.464 --> 00:52:07.054
I want to go and see that barfly-screen man.

00:52:07.114 --> 00:52:08.775
Is it okay?

00:52:08.835 --> 00:52:10.775
Of course, Josie.

00:52:10.835 --> 00:52:11.995
Have fun.

00:52:12.055 --> 00:52:14.646
You're only young once in your life.

00:52:14.706 --> 00:52:16.856
I'm happy by myself.

00:52:16.916 --> 00:52:22.437
Maybe there will be a lovely rich widower sitting next to me on the ghost train.

00:52:22.497 --> 00:52:23.918
Bye, Ron.

00:52:23.978 --> 00:52:27.418
Bye.

00:52:27.478 --> 00:52:31.964
Well, what a holiday.

00:52:32.024 --> 00:52:36.422
I hope the rest of the week is more peaceful and with no more disasters.

00:52:36.482 --> 00:52:39.474
Don't forget, we have to go home in your car.

00:52:39.534 --> 00:52:40.905
That is a disaster.

00:52:40.965 --> 00:52:43.437
Okay, okay, not again.

00:52:43.497 --> 00:52:44.868
Can we change the subject?

00:52:44.908 --> 00:52:45.949
You started it.

00:52:46.009 --> 00:52:48.271
You mentioned disasters, not me.

00:52:48.331 --> 00:52:50.292
You mentioned the car, not me.

00:52:50.352 --> 00:52:52.064
Not so loud.

00:52:52.124 --> 00:52:55.166
Everyone is listening to us.

00:52:55.226 --> 00:52:58.298
What's that in your teacup?

00:52:58.358 --> 00:52:59.939
It's moving.

00:52:59.999 --> 00:53:00.590
What?

00:53:00.650 --> 00:53:01.646
Where?

00:53:01.706 --> 00:53:04.104
Oh no, it's a fly.

00:53:04.164 --> 00:53:05.216
I don't believe it.

00:53:05.276 --> 00:53:07.659
There's a fly swimming in my Earl Grey.

00:53:07.719 --> 00:53:09.021
Do something then.

00:53:09.081 --> 00:53:10.445
Don't just look at it.

00:53:10.505 --> 00:53:11.798
Give me the newspaper.

00:53:11.858 --> 00:53:13.559
No, don't do that.

00:53:13.619 --> 00:53:16.610
Oh, why did you do that?

00:53:16.650 --> 00:53:18.981
You're so stupid.

00:53:19.041 --> 00:53:20.051
I killed the fly.

00:53:20.071 --> 00:53:21.942
Oh, yes, you killed the fly.

00:53:22.002 --> 00:53:25.653
But your whole tea went all over my dress.

00:53:25.673 --> 00:53:26.623
What happened?

00:53:26.683 --> 00:53:28.074
It's not so bad.

00:53:28.134 --> 00:53:28.824
It is.

00:53:28.884 --> 00:53:30.544
Look, I can't wear this.

00:53:30.605 --> 00:53:31.665
You can wash it.

00:53:31.725 --> 00:53:32.395
No problem.

00:53:32.415 --> 00:53:36.042
Why can't you wash it?

00:53:36.102 --> 00:53:41.608
Why is life so difficult with you, Pete?

00:53:41.668 --> 00:53:43.480
I don't know what you mean.

00:53:43.540 --> 00:53:48.752
We came to Blackpool to have a holiday, but so far it isn't happening.

00:53:48.812 --> 00:53:52.574
I'm going back to the hotel to have a rest on the bed.

00:53:52.634 --> 00:53:55.896
Bit of peace and quiet is what I need now.

00:53:55.956 --> 00:53:57.576
I can come with you.

00:53:57.636 --> 00:53:58.336
No, no.

00:53:58.397 --> 00:53:59.677
It's okay.

00:53:59.737 --> 00:54:02.678
You stay here and destroy some more cups.

00:54:02.738 --> 00:54:05.978
You can meet Mum and Josie and then come back to the hotel later.

00:54:06.038 --> 00:54:07.958
If you think that is the best thing to do.

00:54:08.018 --> 00:54:08.589
Yes.

00:54:08.649 --> 00:54:10.270
Yes, definitely.

00:54:10.330 --> 00:54:12.112
OK, Nancy.

00:54:12.172 --> 00:54:14.944
Go to bed if you think it's what you need.

00:54:15.004 --> 00:54:17.565
I think bed is a good idea.

00:54:17.585 --> 00:54:21.068
A very good idea.

00:54:21.128 --> 00:54:24.280
See you later.

00:54:24.341 --> 00:54:26.792
Can I...

00:54:26.852 --> 00:54:28.234
Hey, please.

00:54:28.294 --> 00:54:30.755
Yes, sorry about the cups.

00:54:30.815 --> 00:54:34.148
My wife got angry and had an accident.

00:54:34.208 --> 00:54:38.870
Women.

00:54:38.930 --> 00:54:44.302
Oh, hello, Grant.

00:54:44.362 --> 00:54:46.053
Josephine, not with you.

00:54:46.113 --> 00:54:47.084
Hello.

00:54:47.144 --> 00:54:48.054
Er, no.

00:54:48.114 --> 00:54:50.965
Josephine is licking a ice cream.

00:54:51.025 --> 00:54:52.096
What is the matter?

00:54:52.156 --> 00:54:53.246
My tooth.

00:54:53.306 --> 00:54:55.267
I lost them.

00:54:55.327 --> 00:54:56.588
How did you do that?

00:54:56.648 --> 00:55:03.530
I went on the Dodgeham cars, and this nice widow knocked into me and they went flying into the air.

00:55:03.590 --> 00:55:05.121
How can I find them?

00:55:05.181 --> 00:55:06.161
Oh, dear.

00:55:06.222 --> 00:55:07.656
What a pity.

00:55:07.716 --> 00:55:09.241
Hope you find them.

00:55:09.301 --> 00:55:11.184
You can't eat without them.

00:55:11.244 --> 00:55:13.315
I've spare Paris at home.

00:55:13.376 --> 00:55:14.096
Pity.

00:55:14.156 --> 00:55:16.559
Maybe you can get a straw in the hotel.

00:55:16.619 --> 00:55:18.491
That's a good idea.

00:55:18.531 --> 00:55:19.772
Well, have fun.

00:55:19.832 --> 00:55:22.226
I'm walking around the pleasure beach for a while.

00:55:22.286 --> 00:55:24.007
Nancy is back at the hotel.

00:55:24.067 --> 00:55:24.828
Bye.

00:55:24.888 --> 00:55:29.068
Bye.

00:55:29.128 --> 00:55:33.598
Where's my car?

00:55:33.658 --> 00:55:35.039
It's not in the car park.

00:55:35.099 --> 00:55:36.200
It's stolen.

00:55:36.260 --> 00:55:37.440
Can someone help?

00:55:37.500 --> 00:55:38.671
Where is everyone?

00:55:38.731 --> 00:55:40.572
Where's that Italian manager?

00:55:40.632 --> 00:55:43.944
When you want someone, call the police.

00:55:44.004 --> 00:55:46.184
Nancy?

00:55:46.245 --> 00:55:48.796
Nancy, open the door.

00:55:48.856 --> 00:55:50.026
Throw in the police.

00:55:50.087 --> 00:55:51.978
My car, it's stolen.

00:55:52.038 --> 00:55:53.968
Open the door.

00:55:54.028 --> 00:55:55.739
Where is everyone?

00:55:55.799 --> 00:55:57.660
Are you asleep?

00:55:57.720 --> 00:55:59.401
I don't believe it.

00:55:59.461 --> 00:56:00.542
Where is she?

00:56:00.601 --> 00:56:02.494
Women.

00:56:02.554 --> 00:56:04.686
My mobile.

00:56:04.746 --> 00:56:06.406
I have it in my pocket.

00:56:06.466 --> 00:56:07.607
Nine.

00:56:07.667 --> 00:56:08.658
Nine.

00:56:08.718 --> 00:56:10.558
Nine.

00:56:10.618 --> 00:56:12.610
Hello?

00:56:12.670 --> 00:56:14.550
Yes, it's an emergency.

00:56:14.610 --> 00:56:15.812
Police.

00:56:15.872 --> 00:56:17.662
My car is stolen.

00:56:17.722 --> 00:56:19.684
Hotel Grand Park.

00:56:19.744 --> 00:56:21.364
On the seafront.

00:56:21.424 --> 00:56:27.628
Registration F-H-W-2-9-6-K.

00:56:27.688 --> 00:56:28.948
What?

00:56:29.008 --> 00:56:30.419
My name?

00:56:30.479 --> 00:56:32.314
Um, Britain.

00:56:32.374 --> 00:56:33.478
Pete Britain.

00:56:33.538 --> 00:56:36.199
Come quickly.

00:56:36.260 --> 00:56:39.300
What's the problem, Dad?

00:56:39.360 --> 00:56:41.030
I can hear you from outside.

00:56:41.091 --> 00:56:41.711
The car.

00:56:41.771 --> 00:56:42.381
Stolen.

00:56:42.441 --> 00:56:43.181
God!

00:56:43.241 --> 00:56:44.302
Where's Boris?

00:56:44.362 --> 00:56:45.412
And where's...

00:56:45.472 --> 00:56:46.422
What?

00:56:46.482 --> 00:56:47.312
Who?

00:56:47.372 --> 00:56:48.463
Oh, Boris.

00:56:48.523 --> 00:56:49.223
I don't know.

00:56:49.283 --> 00:56:50.293
In the car.

00:56:50.353 --> 00:56:51.644
Driving the car.

00:56:51.704 --> 00:56:52.944
Come down, Dad.

00:56:53.004 --> 00:56:54.514
Don't get hysterical.

00:56:54.574 --> 00:56:56.455
Boris can't drive the car.

00:56:56.515 --> 00:56:57.626
He's too young.

00:56:57.686 --> 00:56:59.226
He doesn't have a licence.

00:56:59.286 --> 00:57:01.058
What are you talking about?

00:57:01.118 --> 00:57:02.451
Boris doesn't have a license.

00:57:02.511 --> 00:57:03.894
What are you talking about?

00:57:03.954 --> 00:57:05.206
It's a joke, Dad.

00:57:05.266 --> 00:57:06.358
Stay cool.

00:57:06.418 --> 00:57:09.052
I am cool.

00:57:09.112 --> 00:57:10.936
The police are here.

00:57:10.996 --> 00:57:16.662
Come on.

00:57:16.722 --> 00:57:24.412
Good morning, sir.

00:57:24.472 --> 00:57:25.964
Oh, no.

00:57:26.024 --> 00:57:26.956
It's you.

00:57:27.016 --> 00:57:28.908
Yes, it's me, sir.

00:57:28.968 --> 00:57:30.801
Nice to see you again, sir.

00:57:30.861 --> 00:57:31.692
Hmm.

00:57:31.752 --> 00:57:33.626
What's the problem, sir?

00:57:33.686 --> 00:57:34.546
My car.

00:57:34.606 --> 00:57:35.869
It's not in the car park.

00:57:35.929 --> 00:57:37.230
It's a classic car.

00:57:37.290 --> 00:57:40.284
It's probably sold by now and is out of the country.

00:57:40.344 --> 00:57:42.417
I don't think so, sir.

00:57:42.477 --> 00:57:43.728
How do you know?

00:57:43.788 --> 00:57:45.480
It's a very special car.

00:57:45.540 --> 00:57:47.032
There aren't many left in the world.

00:57:47.092 --> 00:57:48.703
Don't worry, sir.

00:57:48.764 --> 00:57:50.225
Of course I worry.

00:57:50.285 --> 00:57:51.517
It's my car.

00:57:51.577 --> 00:57:53.819
We found your car, sir.

00:57:53.879 --> 00:57:55.652
Twenty minutes ago.

00:57:55.712 --> 00:57:56.692
Yes?

00:57:56.752 --> 00:57:57.784
Wonderful.

00:57:57.844 --> 00:57:58.764
Where is it?

00:57:58.824 --> 00:58:00.966
Where we found it, sir.

00:58:01.026 --> 00:58:03.967
Yes, well, one mile from here.

00:58:04.027 --> 00:58:06.868
It broke down in the middle of the high streets.

00:58:06.928 --> 00:58:10.940
There is a three-mile traffic jam behind it, sir.

00:58:11.000 --> 00:58:19.074
No one can get into the car to move it because your mad dog attacks anyone who tries to get into the car.

00:58:19.134 --> 00:58:20.494
Sastic.

00:58:20.554 --> 00:58:22.455
My car is OK.

00:58:22.515 --> 00:58:29.185
We would be very grateful if you could come and move your car, sir, before we shoot your mad beast.

00:58:29.245 --> 00:58:30.627
You can't shoot Boris.

00:58:30.687 --> 00:58:31.528
We can.

00:58:31.588 --> 00:58:33.221
We certainly can.

00:58:33.281 --> 00:58:43.688
So both of you come with me in my car now, please.

00:58:43.748 --> 00:58:51.570
Where is everyone?

00:58:51.630 --> 00:58:53.121
It's late.

00:58:53.181 --> 00:58:55.421
Don't worry, Nancy.

00:58:55.481 --> 00:58:57.332
Oh, here comes your mother.

00:58:57.392 --> 00:58:58.932
Oh, Nancy.

00:58:58.992 --> 00:59:00.533
I can't find them.

00:59:00.593 --> 00:59:02.093
I lost my teeth.

00:59:02.153 --> 00:59:03.934
What are you talking about?

00:59:03.994 --> 00:59:05.444
Didn't Pete tell you?

00:59:05.504 --> 00:59:08.565
No, I was busy.

00:59:08.625 --> 00:59:10.035
What happened?

00:59:10.095 --> 00:59:11.305
Where's Josephine?

00:59:11.365 --> 00:59:13.886
She went off to have a bitter ice cream.

00:59:13.946 --> 00:59:15.216
Where is she now?

00:59:15.276 --> 00:59:17.247
And where is Pete?

00:59:17.307 --> 00:59:18.888
What a holiday.

00:59:18.908 --> 00:59:21.620
This nice widower helped me look.

00:59:21.680 --> 00:59:22.330
Who?

00:59:22.390 --> 00:59:23.680
Where?

00:59:23.741 --> 00:59:25.492
For your lost teeth.

00:59:25.552 --> 00:59:30.845
Yes, I crashed on the Dodging Cars and they came out of my mouth.

00:59:30.905 --> 00:59:33.146
How terrible mother.

00:59:33.206 --> 00:59:34.897
There you are.

00:59:34.957 --> 00:59:37.278
Oh, there you both are.

00:59:37.339 --> 00:59:38.569
What happened?

00:59:38.629 --> 00:59:40.490
I can ask you the same question.

00:59:40.551 --> 00:59:43.090
Where were you when I knocked on the bedroom door?

00:59:43.150 --> 00:59:45.489
It's stolen with Boris inside.

00:59:45.550 --> 00:59:47.861
So now you must buy a new car.

00:59:47.921 --> 00:59:49.262
No, it's okay.

00:59:49.322 --> 00:59:51.234
The police found it in the High Street.

00:59:51.294 --> 00:59:52.444
What a pity.

00:59:52.504 --> 00:59:54.856
And where were you this afternoon, Josephine?

00:59:54.917 --> 00:59:57.658
I thought you were going on the ghost train with your grandmother.

00:59:57.718 --> 01:00:00.250
You weren't with your grandmother, Josephine?

01:00:00.310 --> 01:00:02.422
No, I, er...

01:00:02.482 --> 01:00:04.384
went shopping for clothes.

01:00:04.444 --> 01:00:08.170
Your grandmother told me you went for an ice cream.

01:00:08.230 --> 01:00:10.045
That as well.

01:00:10.106 --> 01:00:11.938
I am confused.

01:00:11.998 --> 01:00:13.982
I don't know where I am.

01:00:14.042 --> 01:00:16.426
Is this all so important?

01:00:16.486 --> 01:00:19.580
I think we all need a nice cup of tea.

01:00:19.640 --> 01:00:21.214
You're right Mum.

01:00:21.274 --> 01:00:27.070
Luigi, can we all have some tea and cakes in the restaurant, please?

01:00:27.130 --> 01:00:29.531
Yes, of course.

01:00:29.591 --> 01:00:34.914
And can you book us a table in your restaurant for a celebration tomorrow evening?

01:00:34.974 --> 01:00:36.764
Of course, Nancy.

01:00:36.824 --> 01:00:38.375
What is the occasion?

01:00:38.435 --> 01:00:41.747
It's my birthday, but I don't feel like celebrating.

01:00:41.807 --> 01:00:45.499
Perhaps something revealing is going to happen.

01:00:45.559 --> 01:00:47.760
And make it truth.

01:00:47.820 --> 01:00:49.918
Are you talking about?

01:00:49.978 --> 01:00:53.916
I don't understand women.

01:00:53.976 --> 01:00:55.416
Wait and see!

01:00:55.476 --> 01:01:08.552
Wait and see!

01:01:08.612 --> 01:01:12.304
This is nice, isn't it?

01:01:12.324 --> 01:01:14.655
I don't like the food.

01:01:14.715 --> 01:01:16.776
It's foreign muck.

01:01:16.837 --> 01:01:19.238
I don't understand the menus.

01:01:19.298 --> 01:01:20.768
Stop moaning.

01:01:20.828 --> 01:01:22.489
This is my birthday.

01:01:22.549 --> 01:01:25.180
You're having a nice time, aren't we?

01:01:25.240 --> 01:01:28.361
I can't eat this meat without my teeth.

01:01:28.421 --> 01:01:30.602
This straw doesn't help.

01:01:30.662 --> 01:01:32.143
Mother, please.

01:01:32.203 --> 01:01:34.114
Don't make that noise.

01:01:34.174 --> 01:01:37.315
Well, it's difficult to eat, Nancy.

01:01:37.375 --> 01:01:40.346
Can I ask the waiter to cut up my meat?

01:01:40.406 --> 01:01:41.726
No, you can't.

01:01:41.786 --> 01:01:44.206
Let me do it.

01:01:44.266 --> 01:01:47.586
Do you like your meal, Pete?

01:01:47.646 --> 01:01:51.048
It's okay, but it's very expensive.

01:01:51.108 --> 01:01:54.559
Like a fair fish and chips.

01:01:54.579 --> 01:01:57.220
I thought this would be nice for your birthday.

01:01:57.281 --> 01:01:58.539
Yes, dear.

01:01:58.599 --> 01:02:00.257
Thank you, dear.

01:02:00.277 --> 01:02:01.508
Oh, look over there!

01:02:01.568 --> 01:02:02.228
Where, Mum?

01:02:02.288 --> 01:02:03.098
There!

01:02:03.158 --> 01:02:06.339
It's the lovely widower who helped me yesterday.

01:02:06.359 --> 01:02:07.930
Which one, Grand?

01:02:07.990 --> 01:02:08.590
Him!

01:02:08.650 --> 01:02:09.860
Opposite her!

01:02:09.920 --> 01:02:11.971
Next to the other man with the shirt.

01:02:12.031 --> 01:02:14.712
Ooh, Gary!

01:02:14.772 --> 01:02:16.552
Mum, stop it!

01:02:16.612 --> 01:02:18.113
Stop waving!

01:02:18.173 --> 01:02:19.994
Your mother is impossible.

01:02:20.054 --> 01:02:21.454
Do something, Nancy.

01:02:21.514 --> 01:02:23.156
What do you suggest?

01:02:23.216 --> 01:02:26.708
Tying her to the chair and potting her sock in her mouth is a good idea.

01:02:26.728 --> 01:02:29.189
He's coming to our table.

01:02:29.249 --> 01:02:31.200
Oh, lovely.

01:02:31.260 --> 01:02:33.421
Oh, it has my teeth.

01:02:33.481 --> 01:02:35.202
It found my teeth.

01:02:35.262 --> 01:02:37.634
Oh, thank you so much.

01:02:37.694 --> 01:02:40.005
Let me give you a big kiss.

01:02:40.065 --> 01:02:42.416
Oh, stop it mother!

01:02:42.476 --> 01:02:43.436
Sit down!

01:02:43.496 --> 01:02:45.196
Everyone in the restaurant is watching!

01:02:45.216 --> 01:02:46.286
Bit of so!

01:02:46.346 --> 01:02:47.077
Happy!

01:02:47.137 --> 01:02:50.888
I have my teeth!

01:02:50.948 --> 01:02:53.498
Ah!

01:02:53.558 --> 01:02:55.529
Now I can eat this meat.

01:02:55.589 --> 01:02:57.749
Oh, that's much better.

01:02:57.809 --> 01:03:00.330
I suddenly don't feel like eating anymore.

01:03:00.390 --> 01:03:01.666
Sorry, Nancy.

01:03:01.726 --> 01:03:03.244
I understand.

01:03:03.304 --> 01:03:05.826
Why have you stopped eating, Pete?

01:03:05.886 --> 01:03:08.068
I feel so hungry now.

01:03:08.128 --> 01:03:09.459
Give me your plate.

01:03:09.519 --> 01:03:11.251
I can eat your dinner as well.

